interpres ex Graeco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpogravfesqai</FOREIGN> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">et professio,</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpografhú</FOREIGN>  ver. 2, voces haud vulgati jam usus, sed
revera censuales, ut ab eruditis notatum, et quasi
technicae. Et quidem elegantius, inquit Boysius,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut
profiterentur,</HI>  quam,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut describerentur,</HI>  hoc praesertim
in loco, ubi,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toú ajpogravfesqai,</FOREIGN>  non ad censum agentes,
sed ad eos, qui censentur, refertur. Sic,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpografhú,</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0129C"></COL> eos, qui censentur, respiciens, est proprie,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">professio.</HI></P> <P COM="0129">Luc. cap. V, 14, Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">offers munus.</HI>  Tertullianus
