23. Et dimissa
turba, ascendit
in montem
solus orare.
Vespere autem
facto solus erat
24. ibi: Navicula
autem <NOTE N="(a)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0237" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0237"></COL> Addit  <HI REND="ITALIC">jam:</HI>  et ita textus Graecus,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hædh.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  jam †
in medio mari
jactabatur <NOTE N="(b)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0237" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0237"></COL> Ita et textus Graecus,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpoú twðn kumavtwn.</FOREIGN></NOTE> 
a fluctibus †:
erat enim
illis ventus 
25. adversarius.
Quarta
autem vigilia
noctis, venit ad
eos <NOTE N="(c)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0237" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0237"></COL> Additur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesus,</HI>  juxta textum Graecum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ 1Ihsouðû.</FOREIGN></NOTE>  Jesus †
ambulans supra
26. mare. Videntes <NOTE N="(d)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0237" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0237"></COL> Ita et cod. Cant.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev.</FOREIGN></NOTE> 
autem † illum,
turbati sunt,
