respiciens retro,
 <NOTE N="(e)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0587" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0587"></COL> Lege  <HI REND="ITALIC">et mittens.</HI></NOTE>  mittit manum
in aratrum †,
aptus est regno
Dei.</P> <CAPTION COM="0588">CAPUT X. <NOTE TYPE=chad ANCHORED=N COM="0588" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0588"></COL> Footnotes containing readings from the Codex Vindebonensis which depart from the Vulgate have been keyed in a block following the Codex Brixianus.</NOTE></CAPTION> <P COM="0588">1. <NOTE N="(f)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0587" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0587"></COL> Ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">designavit,</HI>  deest  <HI REND="ITALIC">post haec,</HI>  etiam in cod. Cant.</NOTE>  Dessignavit †
autem Jesus
et alios LXX.
et misit illos
