15. Et tu Cafarna . . .
 <NOTE N="(d)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y ED="Blanchinus, Josephus" COM="0589" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0589"></COL> Ita et cod. Cant.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhú eåwû</FOREIGN>  (numquid usque)  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujranouð uJywqhvshé, hÞ eåwû
aåédou katabhvshé</FOREIGN> 
( <HI REND="ITALIC">descendes</HI> ); tex. Gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katabibasqhvsh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">demergeris.</HI></NOTE>  quid us . . . . . . .
