omnes S. Augusti habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia dicit ei.</HI></P> <P COM="0862"><COL N="0862C"></COL> Joan. XIV, 17. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nec novit.</HI>  Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nec
agnoscit;</HI>  et ita S. Ambrosius in lib. I, de Spir. sanct.
cap. 4, pag. 611, et in Exposit. Evang. secund. Luc.;
Veronen. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nec cognoscit.</HI></P> <P COM="0862">Luc. I, 2. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ministri fuerunt verbi.</HI>  Budaeus,
Hamm., Cappell., Vall., Vatab., Pisc., Gemar.
et ex antiquis Origenes in Luc. homil. I, Ambrosius,
Euthymius hic, Hieronymus Praefatione in Matthaeum,
et text. Graec.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Uphrevtai genovmenoi touð lovgou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Ministri
fuerunt verbi.</HI></P> <P COM="0862">Luc. II, 49. Brixian., Vercellen., Veronen. et Gat.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">nescitis,</HI>  etc. Tertullianus pag. 516,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non scitis.</HI></P> <P COM="0862">Luc. III, 5. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in directum;</HI>  et ita codex
Claromont. S. Irenaei.</P> <P COM="0862">Luc. VII, 42. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis ergo eorum,</HI>  etc. S. Cyprianus,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis illorum,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0862">Luc. XXIV, 24. Brixian., Vercellen., Veronen.,
Corbeien. et Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non viderunt;</HI>  et ita quidam mss.
Div. Bibl. S. Hier. et S. Augustinus in lib. III de
Consensu Evangelistarum tom. III, part. II, pag. 140.</P> <P COM="0862"><COL N="0862D"></COL> Marc. V, 43. Brixian. et Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et jussit illi dari
manducare.</HI>  S. Irenaeus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et jussit ei dare manducare;</HI> 
Clarom. ejusdem S. Irenaei cod. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dari,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0862">Marc. XI, 25. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ad orationem;</HI>  et ita S. Cyprianus
in lib. III Testimoniorum ad Quirinum cap. 22,
pag. 378.</P> <P COM="0862">Matth. XIV, 3. Brixianus et Veronensis legunt,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Fratris sui Philippi.</HI>  Graecus quoque post illa verba,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">fratris sui,</HI>  addit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Philippi,</HI>  ex Marc. VI, 17.</P> <P COM="0862">Joan. III, 5. Deest  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sancto</HI>  in Brixian. et Veronen.;
et ita hodie in omnibus Graecis, et plerisque Latinis
exemplaribus; in Tertul. libro de Baptismo, et libro de
Anima; in S. Cyprian. epist. 73, ad Jubaianum, de
haereticis baptizandis, pag. 187; et in S. Ambros.
lib. III de Spiritu sancto cap. 10, pag. 677.</P> <P COM="0862">Luc. I, 3. Brixian. et Veronen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">omnibus.</HI>  In Graeco
quoque codice est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðsin,</FOREIGN>  id est  <HI REND="ITALIC">omnibus,</HI>  quod Syrus
Interpres ad personas refert, interpretans Lucam,
 <COL N="0863A"></COL> quasi dicat, se assectatum esse oculatos testes, et
ministros: ita non accipit metaphorice verbum
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parhkolouqhkovti,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">assecuto,</HI>  pro assequi mente ea, quae
facta et dicta sunt; sed proprie, pro,  <HI REND="ITALIC">assectari aliquem.</HI></P> <P COM="0863">Luc. I, 35. Deest  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex te,</HI>  in Brixian., Veronen., ut
etiam in pluribus Latinis exemplaribus, in sancti Ambrosii
Exposit. Evang. secund. Lucam pag. 1300, in
nonnullis Biblicis libris Reginae Suecorum, et in Gallicanis
plerisque mss. S. Augustini lib. II de Consensu
Evangelistarum. Verum ea verba leguntur ab
Irenaeo, Tertulliano, Novatiano cap. 19 de Trinitate,
aliisque antiquis scriptoribus, et versionibus Syr. et
Arab. relatis a Millio in edit. text. Graeci.</P> <P COM="0863">Luc. VI, 26. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Prophetis;</HI>  et ita duo libri
mss. Div. Bibl. sancti Hieronymi.</P> <P COM="0863">Luc. IX, 48. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quicumque me recipit, recipit
eum;</HI>  Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quicumque me recipit, non me recipit,
sed eum,</HI>  etc. Veron. et Corbeien.  <HI REND="ITALIC">non me recipit,
sed eum,</HI>  etc. Hilarius Diaconus, qui Ambrosiaster
 <COL N="0863B"></COL> dicitur, in Epist. ad Romanos cap. II, pag. 41,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">qui me recipit, non me recipit, sed eum,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0863">Matth. XXII, 35. In Brixian. et Corbeien. omittuntur
verba illa,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut impleretur, quod dictum est per Prophetam
dicentem: diviserunt sibi vestimenta mea, et
super vestem meam miserunt sortem:</HI>  nec leguntur
apud Origenem, Euthymium, Theophylactum, S. Hilarium;
S. Augustinum lib. II, de Consensu Evangelistarum
tom. III, part. II, pag. 121; Titum Bostrensem;
versiones Syriacam, Copticam, Arabicam,
Aethiopicam; editionem Complutensem, et codices
Graecos manu exaratos quamplurimos relatos in
Variis Lectionibus Millii. Desunt etiam in aliis codd.
praeferentibus Latinam Veterem Vulgatam Italam.
Sunt qui putant, haec ab Joanne in Matthaeum irrepsisse
Librariorum licentia. Ego vero Vulgatae lectionem
sequor.</P> <P COM="0863">Joan. X, 22. Brixian. et Corbeien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Facta est autem
Dedicatio in Hierosolymis.</HI>  Nomen illud,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0863C"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgkaivnia,</FOREIGN>  derivatur ab  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgkainizein,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">de novo aliquid
facere,</HI>  quo verbo LXX Interpretes reddunt verbum.
Hebraeum  <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0120863A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT>   <HI REND="ITALIC">initiavit, dedicavit,</HI>  et apud dictos Interpretes
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgkaivnia, ejgkaivnisiû, ejgkainismovû,</FOREIGN>  id est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">innovationes,
innovatio.</HI>  Verbum autem Hebraeum, sicut
et nomen, usurpantur in Veteri Testamento de quavis
Dedicatione sive prima, sive instaurata, puta
cum nova domus incipit habitari; attamen usu factum
videtur, ut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgkaivnia,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">encaenia,</HI>  accepta sint pro
aliqua renovatione, sive instauratione Templi; quod
deducimus ex Hebraeorum Kalendario, in quo, duo
tantum memorantur celebranda Encaenia Templi,
nec mentio fit Salomonicorum: priora in mense
Kasleu, vigesima quinta die, qua Machabaei restituerunt
Altare Holocaustorum; et ideo  <CITN>(ut I Machab. IV,
59, legimus)</CITN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">statuit Judas, et fratres ejus, et universa
Ecclesia Israel, ut agatur dies Dedicationis,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnkainismouð,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Altaris in temporibus suis ab anno in annum per
dies octo, a quinta et vigesima die mensis Casleu cum
 <COL N="0863D"></COL> laetitia et gaudio.</HI>  Altera encaenia, quae reperiuntur
in Kalendario Judaeorum, Dedicatio est, sive instauratio
Templi facta sub Zorobabele in mense Adar,
ut videre est apud Esdram, cap. VI, vers. 16.</P> <P COM="0863">Joan. XI, 56. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid vobis videtur? quia non
veniet ad diem festum?</HI>  Sunt qui Graecum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Tiv dokeið
uJmiðn_ oåti ouj mhú eælqhé eijû thún eJorthún</FOREIGN> ; cum interrogatione
legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid vobis videtur? annon veniet ad
diem festum?</HI></P> <P COM="0863">Matth. XIII, 45. Brixian. et Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">negotianti;</HI>  et
ita S. Cyprian. in lib. III Testimon. ad Quirinum
pag. 372, et in lib. de Opere et Eleemosynis, in aliquibus
mss; item S. Ambrosius in lib. II de Abraham,
cap. 9, pag. 343.</P> <P COM="0863">Matth. XXVII, 40. In Brixian. et Corbeien. omittitur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vah;</HI>  et ita in textu Graeco, et in S. Augustini
lib. III de Consen. Evangel. tom. III, part. II, p.
127.</P> <P COM="0863"><COL N="0864A"></COL> Matth. XIII, 46. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui inveniens unam praetiosam
margaritam.</HI>  S. Cyprianus in lib. de Opere et
Eleemosynis pag. 305,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi autem invenit pretiosam
margaritam,</HI>  omissa voce  <HI REND="ITALIC">una,</HI>  quae deest pariter in
Vercellen., Veron. et San-Germanen.</P> <P COM="0864">Matth. XX, 15. Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haud non licet mihi facere
de meum quod volo?</HI>  Veteres libri quidam ferunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aut
non licet mihi, quod volo facere de re mea?</HI>  Graecus,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>3H oujk eæxestiv moi poihðsai oå qevlw ejn toiðû ejmoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Aut non
licet mihi facere quod volo in meis?</HI>  et ita Syr. et Antiqua
Vulgata. S. August. in serm. 87 habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non
licet mihi quod volo, facere de meo?</HI></P> <P COM="0864">Joan. III, 3. Brixian. et Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">natus fuerit,</HI>  et ita
aliqui mss. Latini codices relati in Divin. Bibliothec.
S. Hieronymi, pressius Graeco textui.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. VIII, 12. Brixian. et Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non ambulavit;</HI> 
Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non ambulabit.</HI>  S. Ambrosius in lib. de
Fide Orthodoxa contra Arianos, cap. 2, pag. 350,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">non ibit.</HI></P> <P COM="0864">Joan. VIII, 54. Brixian., Gat. et Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">noster est;</HI>  et
 <COL N="0864B"></COL> ita Graeca quaedam exemplaria, et duo mss. libri
Lat. relati in Divin. Bibliothec. S. Hieronymi.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. IX, 12. Brixian. et Veronen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dixerunt autem
ei.</HI>  Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dixerunt ergo ei;</HI>  et ita quidam mss.
codices in Divin. Bibliothec. S. Hieronymi.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. X. 29. Brixian., Vercellen. et Veronen.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">rapere illud,</HI>  etc. (Veron. omittit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">illud</HI> ). S. Ambrosius
in lib. III de Spiritu sancto cap. 16, pag. 689,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">rapere ea,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. XX, 31. Brixian. et Veronen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesus Christus
est Filius Dei.</HI>  S. Irenaeus quoque legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesus est
Filius Dei.</HI></P> <P COM="0864">Joan. XI, 50. Brixian. et Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">expedit nobis;</HI>  et
ita Graecus,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJmiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nobis.</HI></P> <P COM="0864">Joan. XII, 7. Brixian., Veronen. et Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sine,</HI>  etc.;
et ita duo mss. Divin. Bibliothec. S. Hieronymi, et
S. Gaudentius in sermon. 13, pag. 153 postremae
Editionis.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. XV, 2. Brixian., Veronen. et Corbeien.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut
 <COL N="0864C"></COL> fructum plurimum adferat.</HI>  S. Hilarius in Tract. in
psalm. XI, tom. I, pag. 87,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut fructum ampliorem
ferat.</HI>  Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut fructum ampliorem adferat.</HI></P> <P COM="0864">Joan. XVIII, 11. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non bibam,</HI>  etc. et ita
S. Hilarius in tractatu in psal. CXXXVIII, tom. I, pag.
508 et in libro X de Trinitate num. 30. Corbeien.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">nonne bibam,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. XX, 31. Brixian., Veronen. et Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vitam
aeternam;</HI>  et ita S. Irenaeus.</P> <P COM="0864">Luc. I, 51. Brixian., Veronen., Corbeien. et
Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">memorari;</HI>  et ita vetus Interpres, teste Millio
in Proleg. ac quidam libri mss. Bibliorum relati in
Div. Biblioth. S. Hieronymi. S. Irenaeus quoque in
lib. III contra Haereses tom. I, pag. 185, habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">reminisci.</HI></P> <P COM="0864">Luc. II, 38. Brixian., et Veronen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hierusalem;</HI>  et
ita vetustissimus Bibliorum codex Corbeiensis, et
alii plures Latini libri. Item S. Irenaeus in lib. III
contra Haereses, tom. I, pag. 187, et S. Augustinus
 <COL N="0864D"></COL> in lib. II de Consensu Evangelistarum tom. III, part.
II, pag. 38. Corbeien. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jerusalem.</HI>  Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in
Hierusalem.</HI>  et ita Graecus textus.</P> <P COM="0864">Luc. VII, 37. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">discubuit;</HI>  Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">accumbere;</HI> 
Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">recubuit;</HI>  Gat. et Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">accubuit:</HI> 
et ita S. Ambrosius, et plurimi mss. libri in Div.
Bibl. S. Hieronymi.</P> <P COM="0864">Luc. IX, 29. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">me confusus fuerit . . . .
confundet eam;</HI>  Vercellen.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">confusus fuer. . me. . . .
. . . . . . . fundet</HI>  . . . . . . . S. Ambrosius in epist.
class. II, tom. II, pag. 1077,  <HI REND="ITALIC">me confusus fuerit. . . .
confundar et ego eum,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0864">Joan. IX. 61. Brixian.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed primum permitte mihi
renuntiare his, qui,</HI>  etc., et ita S. Augustinus in lib.
II, de Consens. Evangelist. tom. III, part. II, p. 55.
Corb. Bibl.  <HI REND="ITALIC">iis, qui,</HI>  etc., conformiter S. Augustino
in Speculo de Evangel. sec. Lucam tom. III, part. I,
p. 769.</P></DOC> <DOC NAME="Epistola altera - descriptio codicis" AUTHOR="Blanchinus, Josephus" SECOND=YES TEMPSTAT=MOD COM="0864"><COL N="0865"></COL> <HEAD TYPE=main COM="0865">EPISTOLA BLANCHINI ALTERA.
DESCRIBITUR CODEX MS. GRAECO-LATINUS EVANGELIORUM ET ACTORUM, IN BIBLIOTHECA CANTABRIGIENSI ASSERVATUS.</HEAD> <P COM="0865"><COL N="0865A"></COL> Cl. ac doctissimo viro Philippo abbati Garbellio patricio
Brixiano Joseph Blanchinus Veronensis S.
P. D.</P> <P COM="0865">Non es nescius, Garbelli doctissime, quantam Sacrarum
litterarum cultores perceperint utilitatem
ex insigni illa editione  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vulgatae Antiquae Latinae et
Italae Versionis Evangelii secundum Matthaeum, e vetustissimis
erutae Monumentis, studio et labore D.
Joannis Martianay, Presbyteri Benedictini e Congregatione
S. Mauri,</HI>  quam ipse primum Parisiis anno
1695 litterario orbi tradidit. Quod quidem vel ex
eo aperte cognosci potest, quod ubique Liber ille ita
feliciter exceptus est, ut venalis hodierna die apud
nostros Italos bibliopolas minime reperiatur; quamvis
nullus exsistat Divinarum Scripturarum studio
 <COL N="0865B"></COL> incensus, qui ejus lectione carere ullo modo possit.
Quare in Prolegomenis hujus Evangeliarii Quadruplicis,
quoniam mihi opus erat de antiqua Itala versione
Latina multa praefari, ne forte viderer aliquibus
rem a sapientissimo Martianaeo multo diligentius,
majorique cum dignitate, quam de me polliceri
auderem, jam actam, agere, existimavi longe melius
huic editioni consultum, et a me prudentius factum
iri, si te, aliosque Italae versionis amatores invitassem
 <NOTE N="(a)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0865" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0865D"></COL> Vide Prolegomena, col. 0000 et seq.</NOTE>  ad legenda Prolegomena ejusdem Martianaei,
qui illud argumentum singulari eruditione tractavit.
Nunc ergo ad ostendendum, Italam, quae erat
verborum Graecorum tenacior, cum perspicuitate
sententiae, nostro Evangeliario quadruplici contineri,
Graecum originalem textum, in antiquioribus mss.
 <COL N="0865C"></COL> libris praeservatum, adeamus.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si enim,</HI>  inquiebat
S. Hieronymus, ad Damasum scribens,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Latinis exemplaribus
fides est adhibenda, respondeant quibus? tot
enim sunt exemplaria pene, quot codices. Sin autem
veritas est quaerenda de pluribus, cur non ad Graecam
originem revertentes, ea, quae vel a vitiosis Interpretibus
male reddita, vel a praesumptoribus imperitis emendata
perversius, vel a librariis dormitantibus aut addita
sunt, aut mutata, corrigimus?</HI>  Et paulo post:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec praesens Praefatiuncula pollicetur quatuor tantum
Evangelia,</HI>  etc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">codicum Graecorum emendata
collatione, sed Veterum.</HI>  Sanctus quoque Augustinus
in lib. II de Doctrina Christiana eamdem regulam tradit.
De Italae versionis interprete, ope Latinorum
codicum emendando, non est meum statuere, verene
 <COL N="0865D"></COL> aliqui sentiant, an secus. At illud meum est multis
ostendere, aequum esse mihi concedi, ut ego de
Itala non minus tuto judicare possim, ex Graecorum
verborum tenacitate, cum perspicuitate sententiae.
Millii editionem N. T. tu jam legendo, et pervolvendo
trivisti: cum autem pleraque illorum, quae contulit,
Exemplaria, pervetera esse constet, nec quisquam
 <COL N="0866A"></COL> adhuc, quod sciam, si Montfauconium, paucosque
alios excipias, cujus sint aetatis, formaeque, prodiderit;
non alienum putavi testari tibi, quid de illis
opiner. Codicem Evangeliorum Cantabrigiensem
Graeco-Latinum antea describam ex eodem Millio.
Et quamvis sint illae membranae per aliquos
vel Ogygiae, numquam tamen propter eas adducar,
ut aliquem versum mei Quadruplicis Evangeliarii
castigem; quoniam, si eas quandoque sequare, falleris,
aut falles. Est equidem Codex ille antiquissimus,
sed mendosus, ut caeteri. Retinet ipse antiquam
italam, quae tamen cariosas et edentulas lectiones
habet.</P> <P COM="0866">Graeci adeundi sunt codices, sed incorrupti, sine
quibus nemo putet Italam inveniri, ac inventam,
 <COL N="0866B"></COL> absque maculis edi posse. Ego neque Doctoris Maximi
institutum satis laudare, nec aliquorum animositatem
satis mirari queo, quibus labor Hieronymi,
qui aditum sibi ad purissimos Graecos fontes pro
emendando Latino quatuor Evangeliorum codice patefecit,
improbatur; quoniam correctionem suam ex
coenosis illis ac turbulentis Latinorum interpretum
lacunis hauriendam esse non duxit. Censores habuit
Hieronymus sua etiam aetate; qui, ut ejus labori
moras necterent, fidemque detraherent, atque opus
quod aggrediebatur, suspectum Ecclesiis efficerent,
praemonuerunt ignarum vulgus, ut caveret sibi; quoniam
a Latinis exemplaribus recedebat. Sed in
defensione, quam pro se beatissimo papae Damaso
scripsit, ita eum (cupiens amoliri a se illam opinionem)
 <COL N="0866C"></COL> alloquitur, et dicit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Novum Opus facere me
cogis ex veteri; ut post exemplaria Scripturarum toto
Orbe dispersa, quasi quidam arbiter sedeam; et quia
inter se variant, quae sint illa, quae cum Graeca consentiant
veritate, decernam. Pius labor, sed periculosa
praesumptio,</HI>  etc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis enim . . . . cum in manus volumen
assumpserit, et a saliva, quam semel imbibit, viderit,
discrepare quod lectitat, non statim erumpat in
vocem, me falsarium, me clamitans esse sacrilegum,
qui audeam aliquid in veteribus libris addere, mutare,
corrigere? Adversus quam invidiam duplex causa me
consolatur, quod et tu, qui Summus Sacerdos es, fieri
jubes; et verum non esse, quod variat, etiam maledicorum
testimonio comprobatur.</HI>  Et post pauca:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Magnus
hic in nostris codicibus error inolevit; dum, quod in
 <COL N="0866D"></COL> eadem re alius Evangelista plus dixit, in alio, quia minus
putaverint, addiderunt: vel dum eumdem sensum
alius aliter expressit, ille, qui unum e quatuor primum
legerat, ad ejus exemplum caeteros quoque aestimaverit
emendandos. Unde accidit, ut apud nos mista sint
omnia; et in Marco plura Lucae, atque Matthaei; rursum
in Matthaeo plura Joannis, et Marci; et in caeteris
 <COL N="0867A"></COL> reliquorum, quae aliis propria sunt, inveniantur.</HI>  Hoc
etiam codici Brixiano, quem ego tuo munere publici
juris facio, quemque tu. vir cl., insigni epistola tua,
in fronte primae partis hujus editionis impressa, mirifice
illustras, non semel accidit; sed maxime Ms.
Cantabrigiensi Graeco-Latino, cujus hic descriptionem
attexo, antequam tibi sistam praecipuas lectiones
nostri Evangeliarii Quadruplicis, quae cum textu
Graeco Vulgato aliisque decem Romanis codicibus
manu exaratis magis concordant.</P> <CAPTION COM="0867"><HI REND="ITALIC">Descriptio codicis ms. Graeco-latini, Evangeliorum et
Actorum in Bibliotheca Cantabrigiensi asservati</HI> <NOTE N="(a)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0867" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0867D"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Millio in Prolegomenis in novum Test. Graecum,
pag.</HI>  132.</NOTE> .</CAPTION> <P COM="0867">Membranaceus codex est in  <HI REND="ITALIC">quarto</HI>  (uti vulgo loquimur)
grandiori.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Evangelia, et acta Apostolorum</HI> 
 <COL N="0867B"></COL> complectitur. Lacerum, et sexaginta ac sex foliis
mutilatum (e quibus decem circiter supplevit aliunde
recentior calamus), initio belli civilis apud Gallos,
anno 1562, ex coenobio S. Irenaei, Lugduni, postquam
ibi in pulvere diu jacuisset, nactus est Beza:
ipsumque, mox ut absolvisset  <HI REND="ITALIC">majores</HI>  suas, quas
vocat, adnotationes, dono dedit Academiae Cantabrigiensi,
anno 1581, missis una litteris, in quibus
suum aperit de Codice isto consilium. In Academiae
istius Bibliotheca jam repositi variantes lectiones
primus, quod sciam, collegit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Patricius Junius:</HI>  qui
et ipse tradidit eas cl.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Puteanis</HI>  fratribus, Puteani
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Morino,</HI>  etc.; Morinus, seu alius quispiam, Stephano
Curcellaeo. Sed et Usserius exemplar hoc ad editionem
N. Test. anni 1624 Elzevirianam accurate contulit,
 <COL N="0867C"></COL> ejusque varietates, ut et aliorum insuper quindecim
mss. codicum, cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Waltono</HI>  communicavit,
in Bibliorum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poluglwvttwn</FOREIGN>  tomo sexto, sive appendice
reponendas. Exemplar ipsum quod attinet, descriptum
est quidem illud litteris grandiusculis, sive
uncialibus, absque omni verborum distinctione, lineis
non in unam eamdemque longitudinem exporrectis,
sed omnino inaequalibus, longioribus aliis,
aliis brevioribus, velut  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn eiædei stichrwðn,</FOREIGN>  in quibus
sedulo a descriptore cautum est, ut Graeca, et Latina
sibi invicem responderent, verbum fere verbo,
servato plerumque etiam eodem ipso verborum ordine.
Graeca sinistram paginam occupant, dextram
Latina. Periere duo prima folia: ad tertium, sive
paginam quintam, incipit Latina versio  <CITN>(Matth. I,
 <COL N="0867D"></COL> 12)</CITN> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Post transmigrationem autem Babylonis,</HI>  etc.;
ad paginam sextam textus Graecus, cap. I, vers. 20,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paralabeiðn Mariaúm,</FOREIGN>  etc. In Evangeliis,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Matthaeum</HI> 
proxime sequitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joannes,</HI>  idque consilio ipsius Digestoris;
ad calcem enim Matthaei haec habet:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eujaggevlion kataú Matqaiðon ejtelevsqh, aærcetai Eujaggevlion
kataú 1Iwavnnhn.</FOREIGN>  Joannem sequitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">Lucas,</HI>  Lucam  <HI REND="ITALIC">Marcus,</HI> 
 <COL N="0868A"></COL> cum eadem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpigrafhð×</FOREIGN>  ita nempe dispositis libris
istis, ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Apostolorum</HI>  Evangelia praeponerentur Evangeliis
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Apostolicorum,</HI>  quomodo  <HI REND="ITALIC">Marcum,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Lucam,</HI> 
Apostolorum comites vocat Tertullianus <NOTE N="(b)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0867" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0867D"></COL> Lib. IV, contra  <HI REND="ITALIC">Marcion.,</HI>  cap. 2.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Marci</HI> 
Evangelio suffixa est etiam notula, significans post
illud proxime poni librum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Actuum.</HI>  Verum haec est
scribae recentioris. Sequens enim folium, quod
prima facie duodecim postremos versus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Epistolae
tertiae D. Joannis</HI>  exhibet, altera primam partem
capitis primi  <HI REND="ITALIC">Actorum,</HI>  clare indicat Exemplar hoc
jam olim praeter  <HI REND="ITALIC">Evangelia</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Acta,</HI>  complexum
fuisse  <HI REND="ITALIC">Catholicas</HI>  saltem Epistolas. Epistolam vero
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Joannis</HI>  tertiam  <CITN>(praetermissa Judae, nisi tamen in
hoc, ut in aliis quibusdam cod. Epistolae Jacobi
fratris annexa fuerit)</CITN>  subsecutum fuisse librum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Actorum.</HI> 
 <COL N="0868B"></COL> Sic enim ms.:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Epistola Joannis tertia explicit.
Incipit Actus Apostolorum.</HI>  Codici ipsi ad oram (ne
quid intactum praetereamus) ascripta sunt varia:
1 <SUP>o</SUP>  Sectiones  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ammonianae,</HI>  charactere codicis ipsum
probe simulante, sed pleniori nonnihil, ac nigriori.
Solae hic incedunt, et absque comitatu codicis Eusebiani,
quo, ad quam quaeque tabulam spectat,
ostenderetur. Nempe Scriba, cum jam haud adesset
ei minium forte, quo Canonem characteribus rubris
exprimeret, ad mentem  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eusebii</HI> <NOTE N="(c)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0867" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0867D"></COL> Ep. ad Carpianum.</NOTE> , scriptionem ejus
in aliud tempus distulisse videtur, ac postea ex oblivione,
aliaque aliqua causa impeditum fuisse, quominus
ipsam ex instituto describeret. 2 <SUP>o</SUP>  Sparsae hinc
inde voculae  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrchú, tevloû, kaiú levge, wßde sthðke,</FOREIGN>  initium
et finem Lectionum Ecclesiasticarum denotantes, ut
 <COL N="0868C"></COL> et lectionum quarumdam tituli, foeda ac barbara
manu exarati <NOTE N="(d)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0867" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0867D"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cuð gene, annagnosma perh to sabbato, metaimorfoû
annagnosma, annagnosma peri tou kuriakh, annagnosma
eiû tin paraskughn, annagnosma peri toou
sabbatoou eijû thn enkhnhoun ejgkaivnhsin annagnosma peri
to kuriaku twn profoutismatwn, ton apolushon,</FOREIGN>  etc.</NOTE> . 3 <SUP>o</SUP>  Capita quaedam rerum in Evangeliis
tractatarum horrido charactere exarata, aliquando
in marg., saepius autem in summa pagina <NOTE N="(e)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0868" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0868D"></COL> Matth. IX, 35, et X, 1, ubi agitur de morborum
curatione, et electione Apostolorum, exstat haec notula:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tou qerapiei kai ton apostolon,</FOREIGN>  h. e.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periú touð
qerapeuvein, kaiú twðn ajpostolwn</FOREIGN> ; alibi ista:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ton grammatevon kai fariseon,</FOREIGN>  h. e.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periú twðn grammatevwn kaiú
farisaivwn</FOREIGN> ; alibi ista:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Apostolon kai ton uiwn Zebedeon,</FOREIGN> 
i. e.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periú twðn ajpostovlwn, kaiú twðn uiJwðn Zebedaivou.</FOREIGN></NOTE> .
Notulae autem hae, reliquaeque jam dictae, non
unius alicujus descriptoris erant, imo nec unius
saeculi. Aliquae pervetustae sunt, aliae posterioris
paulo aevi, aliae inferioris multo adhuc aetatis; aliae
tantum non hodiernae, seu etiam plane recentes:
singulae Latinorum quorumdam, ut videtur, qui,
animi gratia, vocabulorum portenta ista, uti poterant,
depinxere. Certe textus ipse codicis, Graecus
pariter ac Latinus, est Latini scribae. Quod ostendit
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Simonius</HI> <NOTE N="(f)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0868" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0868D"></COL> Hist. Crit. textus N. T. cap. 30.</NOTE> , ex similitudine characterum textus
utriusque; ex litteris pure Graecis in oppositam versionem
 <COL N="0868D"></COL> admissis; ex ipso instituto codicum hujusmodi
Graeco-Latinorum; qui certe Graecis usui esse
non poterant, (quid enim ipsis cum versione, seu
etiam lingua Latinorum?) sed in Occidentalium omnino
gratiam confecti videntur; ut textu Graeco scilicet
e regione Latini posito, haberent jam, quibus
facultatis aliquid in Graecis, unde et S. codicem melius
 <COL N="0869A"></COL> intelligere eis liceret, et Latina sua, sicubi opus
esset, emendare: denique ex mendis ipsius exemplaris
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>grafikoiðû,</FOREIGN>  quorum aliqua satis clare produnt
amanuensem Latinum; v. gr.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Hrwvdouû, 1Iwavnnouû,
1Iwavnnei, Samaritavnwn, flagellwvsaû, leprwvsou,</FOREIGN>  et ejusmodi
alia. Et jam quidem ad ipsius codicis partes
accedimus.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Latina,</HI>  translationem Italicam exhibet,
qualis tum temporis interpolata ferebatur, ante castigationem
Hieronymi.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Graecum</HI>  vero textum mirifice
corruptum ac depravatum, hujusmodi tamen,
qui originem certe duxerit ex iis fontibus, ex quibus
manavit Italica Versio. Nempe cum exemplaribus
interpretum italorum, et apographis inde deductis
ita omnino actum arbitror. Exemplaria, quibus
interpretes ipsi usi sint, sicut aliquantulum hinc
 <COL N="0869B"></COL> inde passa fuerant a Scribis (id enim ex Syriaca,
aliisque Versionibus aliquibus ad consimiles cum
ipsis Codices adornatis omnino constat): ita in caeteris
egregie referebant Apostolicam dictionem.
Quod autem in Latinorum manus devenerint, deducti
exinde codices mendosi prodiere. Scripti nimirum,
non uti caetera exemplaria Orientis, a scribis
Graecis, linguaeque adeo patriae haud nesciis, qui
textum nitidum fere, probeque curatum emisere;
sed a notariis, quales in Occidente ferebat ista aetas,
misere indoctis et barbaris, qui de libris, quos descripturi
erant, nihil fere norant, praeter ipsas litteras.
Hinc certe tractu temporis, major multo adhuc,
immo vero tandem infinita plane vitiorum, et injectitiarum
lectionum vis Codicibus istis ingruebat. Mox
 <COL N="0869C"></COL> enim, ut e Latinis doctiores aliqui excerpta undecumque
scholia, et insigniores pericopas ascripsissent
ad oram suorum exemplarium, librariis ea transcripturis
illud negotii datum erat, ut universam
hanc farraginem marginalem in Apographi sui corpus
transmitterent. Hujusmodi codices nonnulli hodieque
exstant misere, supraque omnem modum mixti
et maculati. Pervetusti plerique omnes, et eximiae
olim apud Occidentales auctoritatis; eoque certe
majoris, quod interpolatis istis Versionem istam
magis magisque accommodatam dederint Latini alii.
Hinc enim haud quaquam dubitatum erat, quin
Graeca, quibus Latina haec tam probe respondebant,
originarium illum textum integrum et illibatum
exhibuerint, ad quem expressa fuerat Italica
 <COL N="0869D"></COL> versio. Consentientia, sic ut diximus, Graeca haec,
et Latina, primum certe diuque, ut videtur, seorsum,
et in distinctis voluminibus incedebant. Postea autem,
quod apud Occidentales linguae Graecae studium
aliquantulum florere coeperit, eruditis e re visum
est, originarium textum, et versionem sub oculum
simul exhibere; idque vel in eadem pagina, quod in
nonnullis libris factum videmus; vel in diversis, ut
in aliis aliquibus, ac speciatim in hoc Cantabrigiensi.</P> <P COM="0869">Hujus certe, de quo jam agimus, Graeca quod attinet,
vix dici potest, quam supra omnem modum in
iis digerendis licenter se gesserit ac plane lascivierit
Interpolator, quisquis ille. In animo ipsi fuisse
prima fronte credideris, non quidem textum ipsum
 <COL N="0870A"></COL> exhibere, quam ediderant ipsi Evangelistae, sed, observato
dumtaxat S. Textus ordine, ac historia, singula
Evangelia absolutioria ac pleniora reddere. Huc
enim faciunt intromissae in cujusque Evangelii textum
particulae variae, integraeque periodi reliquorum:
huc transposita in unoquoque plurima, ob historiae
claritatem: huc traductae ex Evangeliis  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>perikopaiv</FOREIGN> :
huc interpolationes aliae innumerae. Verum et in
aliam plane sententiam pertrahunt nonnulla vocabula
pro genuinis alia, neutiquam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>shmantikwvtera,</FOREIGN>  adeoque
ad historiae claritatem ac ubertatem nihil conferentia:
mutationes numerorum, casuum, generum, temporum,
passim factae absque omni causa: transpositiones
infinitae, quarum nulla idonea ratio vel fingi poterit:
contracta denique plurima, et excisae hinc inde
 <COL N="0870B"></COL> partes, et quidem totae sententiae, quae mirifice ad
historiae Evangelicae integritatem faciunt. Neutiquam
enim hujusmodi praetermiserit, cui constitutum fuerit
ex unoquoque Evangeliorum conficere integram historiam
Evangelicam, et quasi Diatessaron. Immo vero
certum illud unum, Digestorem hujus textus, in hisce
libris  <HI REND="ITALIC">Evangeliorum,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Actuum</HI>  grassatum fuisse pro
arbitrio; addidisse, sustulisse, mutasse, plane uti
ferebat animus; multoque, ut verbo dicam, labore
illud egisse, ut textus ipsorum Evangelistarum, magna
sui parte, in alium quemdam transformatus incederet.
E locis codicis vitiosis et interpolatis, pauca
dumtaxat hic notabimus. In Evangelio Matthaei, insignis
illa pericope de primis accubitibus coenae  <CITN>(cap.
XX, vers. 28)</CITN>  in interpolatis hisce Graece jam primum
 <COL N="0870C"></COL> apparet:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Umeiðû deú zhteiðte ejk mikrouð aujxhðsai, kaiú ejk
meivzonoû ejlattoneiðsqai×</FOREIGN>  (sic enim legendum)  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijsercovmenoi
deú k. t. l.</FOREIGN>  cujus cum partem posteriorem ex
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Lucae,</HI>  cap. XIV, vers. 8, sumptam nemo non norit,
tum certe prior (quod nondum a quoquam observatum,
quod sciam) ortum habuit ex Graecis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cant.</HI>  ejusdem
Evangelii, cap. XXII, vers. 27, 28:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Egwú gaúr ejn
mevswé uJmwðn hølqon oujc wJû oJ ajnakeivmenoû, all1 wJû oJ diakonwðn
kaiú uJmeiðû hujxhvqhte ejn thðé diakonivaé mou, wJû oJ diakonwðn,
oiJ diamemenhkovteû k. t. l.</FOREIGN>  Cap. XXI, vers. 32, cum in
parobola de filiis duobus in vineam ire jussis, quorum
prior se non iturum dixit, iverit tamen, posterior
iturum se, sed non iverit cum voluntatem Patris
in cod. aliquibus fecisse diceretur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæscatoû,</FOREIGN>  seu posterior
 <CITN>(ut in Latinis mendosis ante Hieronymum)</CITN> ,
 <COL N="0870D"></COL> neque vero aliter haberet exemplar interpolatoris
nostri; quo in Scribas et Sacerdotes, filio posteriori
in ipsius textu comparatos, quadraret haec parabola,
expuncto, fecit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijdovnteû metemelhvqhte,</FOREIGN>  contra omnem
codicum fidem, et sententiam Salvatoris. Apud Marcum,
cap. II. vers. 26, particulam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiú 1Abiavqar touð
ajrcierevwû,</FOREIGN>  ceu historiae veritati haud consentaneam,
sustulit: ut et verba,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðû gaúr puriú aJlisqhvsetai,</FOREIGN>  cap.
IX, vers. 49, quod forte absurda viderentur. Alia
mutavit, Evangelicae veritatis studio. Cap. XV, vers.
25, cum in exemplari suo fuerit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>høn deú wåra trivth,
kaiú ejû tauvrwsan aujtoún,</FOREIGN>  crucifixio vero non nisi ad horam
sextam, seu paulo ante contigerit, ne quid falsi (ut
ipsi videbatur) diceret Evangelista, mutavit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejstauvrwsan</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0871A"></COL> in  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejfuvlasson,</FOREIGN>  ita enim salva omnia. Ejusdem
generis est illud,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû tiv wjneivdisavû me,</FOREIGN>  cap. XV, vers.
34. Haud ferebat quispiam (qui idem apud Matthaeum
dictum esse non jam meminerat) ut Christus, in
cruce pendens, se a Deo derelictum diceret: unde
emollitum voluit  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgkatevleipeû</FOREIGN>  ad marg. per  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wjneivdisaû,</FOREIGN> 
ceu Salvatori apprime congruum, Judaeorum sannis
et contumeliis jam impetito: hoc autem, in codicis
hujus ac aliorum haud dubie aliquem textum irrepsit.
In Evangelio  <HI REND="ITALIC">Lucae,</HI>  ubi insignis prae caeteris
codicis hujus ab aliis variatio est, obtrusit nobis interpolator
novam Christi genealogiam, qua conciliatur
Lucas cum Matthaeo. In hac, pars illa, qua ascenditur
a Josepho ad Salomonem (non ad Nathanem),
Matthaei est, insertis dumtaxat Eliacim, praeter Jechoniam
 <COL N="0871B"></COL> et Josiam,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Amasia</HI>  item,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joas,</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ochosia</HI> 
inter Osiam, et Joram, quos Evangelista iste  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tessaradekavdwn</FOREIGN> 
constituendarum gratia praetermiserat:
reliqua, a Salomone ad Adamum usque, a codicibus
Lucae haud variant. Immanis certe haec est licentia.
Sed et in hunc modum nonnullos jam olim in textu
Evangelico grassatos fuisse testatur Hieronymus
Praef. ad Damasum.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ille,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui unum e quatuor
primum legerat, ad ejus exemplum caeteros quoque
existimavit emendandos.</HI>  Lucae, cap. VI, vers. 4, ad
calcem, exstat hic, et in Steph.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>b'</FOREIGN>  insignis pericope
de homine operante die sabbati, quae desumpta videtur
ex Evangelio secundum Hebraeos. Nescio an et
ex ejusmodi  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dihghvsei</FOREIGN>  aliqua provenerit traditio, quae
occurrit in hoc codice, cap. XXIII, vers. 54, de magnitudine
 <COL N="0871C"></COL> lapidis revoluti ad ostium monumenti
Jesu; ejusmodi eum fuisse, quem  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>movgiû eiækosi ejkuvlion.</FOREIGN> 
In  <HI REND="ITALIC">Actis Apostolorum</HI>  (Evangelium enim  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joannis</HI> 
mittimus, quippe cujus varietates sunt minus notabiles)
textus scatet invectis aliunde scholiis, et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periocaiðû</FOREIGN> 
prolixioribus, quibus historiam Apostolicam
insigniter adauctam et illustratam voluere interpolatores.
Ex his aliqua exstant ad frontem lectionum
Ecclesiasticarum (harum enim initialia, diversa subinde
ab iis, quae exhibet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Praxapovstoloû,</FOREIGN>  nonnullis
in locis in hunc codicem irrepsisse videas). Alibi
etiam quamplurimis amplificatam dedere hanc historiam,
adjectis circumstantiis, excepta una, et altera,
haud in idoneis; si idoneum quidquam dici poterit,
 <COL N="0871D"></COL> quod hujusmodi temeratores in sacrum textum
intruserint de suo.</P> <P COM="0871">Verum utcumque mire interpolata sint hujusce
codicis Graeca; cum tamen in multis retineant puritatem
primaevorum, unde deducta sunt, fontium,
copiam certe haud exiguam exhibent genuinarum
lectionum, a receptis hodiernis discrepantium. De
 <COL N="0872A"></COL> iis, quas  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cantabrig.</HI>  cum aliis codd. communes habet,
non loquimur: hic eas dumtaxat attingemus,
quae in uno hoc, quod sciam, occurrunt exemplari
Graeco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Cwlouúû, tuflouúû, kullouúû.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Matth.</HI>  cap. XV,
vers. 30, abest a nostro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kwfouvû,</FOREIGN>  inclusum scilicet
in sequentibus  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eJtevrouû pollouvû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0872"><FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eijû ajpavnthsin touð numfivou kaiú thðû nuvmfhû,</FOREIGN>  cap. XXV,
vers. 1; sic et Vulgata, Syr. ac Latini; nec dubito
quin ita Matthaei Interpres. Sed, quod infra de sponsi
solius occursu fiat mentio, neque nisi sponsi dumtaxat
occursus memoretur, in posterioribus codd.
delebant illud  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú thðû nuvmfhû</FOREIGN>  Graeci, seu perperam
ab antiquis additum.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Apoú touð aiåmatoû touvtou</FOREIGN>  ( <HI REND="ITALIC">a
sanguine hujus,</HI>  Cant. Lat.), cap. XXVII, vers. 24,
addito  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð dikaivou.—1Arguvrion iJkanoún,</FOREIGN>  cap. XXVIII,
 <COL N="0872B"></COL> vers. 12, cum  <HI REND="ITALIC">Steph.</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>b',</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Cant.</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vulg.</HI>  omnino recte.
Sed cum supra in Graeco in cap. praecedenti sit perpetuo
plurale  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrguvria</FOREIGN>  et, quod magis, paulo infra
v. 15, milites accepisse dicantur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrguvria,</FOREIGN>  haud mirum,
si studiosi jam olim in margine fecerint  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrguvria
iJkanav</FOREIGN>  hoc loco; quod mox admiserunt scribae in textum.
— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Metaú twðn telwnwðn kaiú aJmartwlwðn ejsqivei,</FOREIGN>  Marc.
cap. II, vers. 16, recte; et, ut arbitror, respondent
ad praecedens  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijdoúnteû aujtoún ejsqivonta.—Kaiú oiJ farisaiðoi
ejphrwvthsan aujtoún,</FOREIGN>  cap. X, vers. 2.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Proselqovnteû,</FOREIGN>  ante
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ farisaiðoi</FOREIGN>  quod in nostris jam omnibus, Matthaei
est.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú eærcetai eijû 1Ierivcw,</FOREIGN>  cap. X, vers. 46. Ita in
singulari etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">Lucas,</HI>  Marci assiduus sectator. Plurale
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eærcontai,</FOREIGN>  factum videtur ex Matthaeo.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>7Hn deú
toú pavsca metaú duvo hJmevraû,</FOREIGN>  cap. XIV, vers. 1. Ita habent
 <COL N="0872C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Italica</HI>  et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Saxon.</HI> — <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>OiJ aJmartwloiú aJmartwloiðû
daneivzousin, iåna ajpolavbwsi,</FOREIGN>  cap. VI, vers. 34.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Apolavbwsi</FOREIGN> 
simpliciter, ut in priori parte commatis.—
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Upoú ejqnwðn aæcriû ouß plhrwqwðsin,</FOREIGN>  cap. XXI, vers. 24,
gentes scilicet, conformiter D. Paulo, apud quem
occurrit haud semel  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>plhvrwma twðn ejqnwðn.</FOREIGN> — <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Ouætiû ejstiún
oJ profhvthû,</FOREIGN>  Joann. cap. VI, vers. 14.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>4Opou eæfagon
toún aærton,</FOREIGN>  cap. VI, vers. 23; mox,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujcaristhvsontoû
touð Kurivou.</FOREIGN>  Verum missis istis, ad codicis Latina
properemus. Illa vero (quae ad Italicae versionis
exemplar aliquod descripta diximus) cum in plerisque
accurate ad textum Graecum accommodarit
Digestor Operis, retento eodem verborum quantumcumque
transpositorum, ordine, et quidem vitiis ipsis
 <COL N="0872D"></COL> sui codicis; ubi enim deficiunt Graeca (quod ob
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJmoiotevleuton,</FOREIGN>  scribaeque incuriam innumeris in locis
accidit), deficiunt et Latina, non sine omnis quandoque
sensus dispendio; tum certe ex variis hinc
illinc a Graeco abeuntibus liquet, versionem hanc diversi
ab hoc nostro textus <NOTE N="(a)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0871" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0871D"></COL> Ecce lectiones diversas; priori loco positae,
lectiones codicis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cantabrigiensis</HI>  designant; posteriori,
lectiones codicis graeci, ex quo expressa erat latina
versio Cantabrigiensi obversa.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Elpivzousin, ejlpiouðsin,</FOREIGN> 
Matth. XII, 21;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejlavlei, lalwð,</FOREIGN>  XIII, 13;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prosevcein,
prosevcete,</FOREIGN>  XVI, 12;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejmoún touðto douðnai, ejmoún
douðnai,</FOREIGN>  XX, 23.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>DevrjrJin, trivcaû,</FOREIGN>  Marc, I, 6;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn soiú,
ejn wßé</FOREIGN>  I, 11;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijseporeuvonto, eijsporeuvontai,</FOREIGN>  I, 21;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejperwtwðn,
parakalwðn,</FOREIGN>  I, 40;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>stavcuaû, stavcuh,</FOREIGN>  IV, 28;
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>boskomevnh, boskomevnwn,</FOREIGN>  V, 11;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejqewvrei, qewreið,</FOREIGN>  V,
 <COL N="0872D"></COL> 38;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toiauðta, tauðta,</FOREIGN>  VI, 2;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katevgnwsan, ejmevmyanto,</FOREIGN> 
VII, 2;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajgapaðé, timaðé,</FOREIGN>  VII, 6;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaqarivzei, kaqarivzon,</FOREIGN>  VII,
19;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>foivnissa, surofoivnissa,</FOREIGN>  VII, 26;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejggivzousin, hæggizen,</FOREIGN> 
XI, 1;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proavgw, proavgei,</FOREIGN>  XVI, 7;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prwðtoiû, prwðton,</FOREIGN> 
XVI, 9;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpikefavlaion, khðnson,</FOREIGN>  XII, 14;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wjneivdisaû,
ejgkatavlipeû,</FOREIGN>  XV, 34;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trivth, eåkth,</FOREIGN>  XV, 33.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Boskomevnh,
boskomevnwn,</FOREIGN>  Luc. VIII, 32;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû eJautouvû, eijû auJtovn,</FOREIGN> 
XXII, 65;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujkevti qewreiðte, Ouj qewreiðte.</FOREIGN> —Joan.
XIII, 16;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>trivth, eJkth,</FOREIGN>  XIX, 14;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú oujk ejpivsteusen, kaiú
ejpivsteusen,</FOREIGN>  XX, 8.— <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Eijshðlqen, eijshðlqon,</FOREIGN>  Act. I, 13;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oÝ</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0873D"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gnwstoún, kaiú gnwstovn,</FOREIGN>  I, 19;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>crovnwé wJû, crovnwé, ejn wßé,</FOREIGN> 
I, 21;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavsaû savrkaû, paðsan savrka,</FOREIGN>  II, 17;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejperwthvsw
se, eiøpev moi,</FOREIGN>  V, 8;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj paraggelivaé, paraggelivaé,</FOREIGN>  V, 28;
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dexiaðé, dovxhé,</FOREIGN>  V, 31;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk touð sunedrivou, ejn twðé sunedrivwé,</FOREIGN> 
V, 34;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oußtoi ejstavqhsan, ouÝû eæsthsan,</FOREIGN>  VI, 6;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiå tineû
proseuxavmenoi, kaiú proseuxavmenoi,</FOREIGN>  ibid.;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touðto, tauðta,</FOREIGN> 
VII, 1;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejfugavdeusen, eæfugen,</FOREIGN>  VII, 29;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>suún ceiriv, ejn ceiriv,</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0874D"></COL> VII, 35;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejphvgagon, ejphvgeiran,</FOREIGN>  XIV, 2;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvtwé, ouåtwé,</FOREIGN> 
XV, 15;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpaggelouðntaû, ajpaggevllontaû,</FOREIGN>  XV, 27;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujqevwû,
aujthðé thðé wåraé,</FOREIGN>  XVI, 18;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>protetagmevnouû, prostetagmevnouû,</FOREIGN> 
XVII, 26;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnqumhvsewû, ejpiqumhvsewû,</FOREIGN>  XVII, 29;
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kataseivsaû, katasteivlaû,</FOREIGN>  XIX, 35;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnomivsamen, ejnovmizon,</FOREIGN> 
XXI, 29.</NOTE>  fuisse, iisque porro
non uno loco glossis et expositionibus Latinorum
 <COL N="0873A"></COL> interpolatam esse, quibus obversa Graeca neutiquam
respondent. Ex. gr. quaenam est significationis affinitas
inter ista,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kullouúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sideratos?</HI>  Mat. c. XV, vers.
30.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kulloiú,</FOREIGN>  in genere  <HI REND="ITALIC">membris debiles, mutilati,
manci.</HI>  Lector quispiam, qui, nescio qua de causa,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kullouúû</FOREIGN>  hic loci, pro illis habuit, quibus debilitas
haec ex sideratione contigerat, exposuit  <HI REND="ITALIC">sideratos.</HI> 
Ejusdem generis sunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>talavntwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">denariorum,</HI>  cap.
XVIII, vers. 24;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>novmisma,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">denarium,</HI>  cap. XXII, vers. 19;
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paraskeuhún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">coenam puram,</HI>  cap. XXVII, vers. 62:
ita enim jam olim dicta est Parasceve. Glossae veteres,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">coena pura,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paraskeuhv.</FOREIGN>  Occurrit phrasis apud
Tertullianum, lib. V adversus Marcion., c. 4, et
Augustinus in Joan. notat,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Parasceven</HI>  a Judaeis sui
temporis usitatius dictam fuisse  <HI REND="ITALIC">coenam puram.</HI>  Cur
 <COL N="0873B"></COL> autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">coena</HI>  haec  <HI REND="ITALIC">pura</HI>  diceretur, rationem hanc reddit
doctissimus  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dufresne,</HI> <NOTE N="(a)" TYPE="foot" ANCHORED=Y COM="0874" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0874D"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Carol. Dufresne</HI>  Glossario Lat., voce  <HI REND="ITALIC">Coena.</HI></NOTE>  non quod careret carnibus,
sed quod religionis et dicis causa fieret. Nam
et  <HI REND="ITALIC">Parascevae</HI>  Judaicae habuere carnes, et nihilominus
dicuntur  <HI REND="ITALIC">coenae purae,</HI>  quod dicis causa coquebantur,
coquunturque hodie pro sabbato, quia in sabbato
coqui non liceat. Haec ille.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Novmisma,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">figuram,</HI> 
Luc. cap. XX, vers. 24.</P> <P COM="0873">Vidimus jam qualia fuerint Graeca, qualia item
Latina hujusce codicis. De Graecis unum illud ultra
quaeritur, an aliqua ex parte castigata fuerint ad
Latinum exemplar? Ea enim erat de libris hujus generis
eruditorum quorumdam nostrae et superioris
aetatis, diserta sententia. Nempe cum mirifice consenserint
ista cum Latinis, contra quam reliqui
 <COL N="0873C"></COL> Graeciae libri, iique optimi, facile ipsis persuasum
erat, ea vel non omnino fuisse Graecae originis, sed
tota, quanta quanta, traducta de Latinis, vel saltem
recensita et emendata fuisse variis sui partibus, ad
Latinam versionem. Sic de ipsis pronuntiant  <HI REND="ITALIC">Erasmus,
Lucas Brugensis, Estius, Grotius,</HI>  alii. De hac
re jam ita videtur. Exscripta erant apud Latinos, ex
librorum ad quos confecta erat Itala versio apographis,
varia Graeca exemplaria, ex ignorantia Scribarum,
doctiorumque e Latinis quorumdam  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periergivaé</FOREIGN> 
(qui mutuata e Graecorum libris scholia, in codices
ex suis descriptos inserenda curabant graviter laesa
et interpolata). Istis mox adaptabatur a quibusdam
Latina versio. Ex hac autem consensione factum est,
ut indocta manus paucula hic inde in textu Graeco
 <COL N="0873D"></COL> ad formam Latinorum, et e Latina versione mutaverit.
Illud enim apparet in Graecis  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cant.</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Hrwvdouû,
1Iwavnnouû, Samaritavnwn,</FOREIGN>  aliaque id genus ad Latinorum
formam confecta sunt. Matth. cap. V, vers. 24,
cum Latinum esset  <HI REND="ITALIC">offeres,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>provsfere</FOREIGN>  mutavit librarius
in  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prosfereiðû.</FOREIGN>  Ea enim ipsi erat secunda persona
futuri.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Katabaiðnon,</FOREIGN>  factum  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katabaivnonta,</FOREIGN>  ob
 <COL N="0874A"></COL> Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">descendentem,</HI>  cap. III, vers. 16; XI, 22, 24,
cum esset in Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quam vobis,</HI>  et vero Graecum esset
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ uJmiðn,</FOREIGN>  ut Latino responderet. Sic cap. ejusdem
vers. 28, factum est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnteû oiÝ kopiwðnteû kaiú pefortismevnoi
ejstev,</FOREIGN>  ob Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">omnes qui laboratis, et onerati estis.</HI> 
Cap. XV, vers. 11, 20, ob Latina obsoleta (sed genuina
interpretis Vulgati)  <HI REND="ITALIC">communicat, communicant,</HI> 
i. e., polluit, polluunt, pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>koinoið, koinouðnta,</FOREIGN> 
reposuit absurde  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>koinwneið, koinwnouðnta</FOREIGN> ; uti et Act.
cap. XXI, vers. 28,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJkoinwvnhse toún aågion tovpon touðton,</FOREIGN> 
ob Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">communicavit locum sanctum hunc.</HI>  Sic Matth.
cap. XVIII, vers. 22,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejbdomhkontavkiû eJptavkiû,</FOREIGN>  ob Lat.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">septies.</HI>  Act. cap. V, vers. 9,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunefwvnhsen</FOREIGN>  (pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunefwnhvqh)
uJmiðn,</FOREIGN>  ob Lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">convenit vobis.</HI>  Mitto alia.</P></DOC> <DOC NAME="Epistola" AUTHOR="Beza, Theodorus" SECOND=YES TEMPSTAT=MOD COM="0874"><COL N="0874B"></COL> <HEAD TYPE=main COM="0874">EPISTOLA THEODORI BEZAE.

 <HI REND="ITALIC">Inclytae modisque omnibus celebratissimae Academiae
Cantabrigiensi,</HI>  etc.</HEAD> <P COM="0874"><HI REND="ITALIC">Quatuor Evangeliorum, et Actorum Apostolorum
Graeco-Latinum exemplar, ex S. Irenaei Coenobio
Lugdunensi ante aliquot annos nactus, mutilum quidem
illud, et neque satis emendate ab initio ubique
descriptum, neque ita ut oportuit habitum (sicut ex paginis
quibusdam diverso charactere insertis, et indocti
cujuspiam Graeci Calogeri barbaris ascriptis quibusdam
notis apparet), vestrae potissimum Academiae,</HI>  etc.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">celeberrimae, dicandum existimavi,</HI>  etc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in cujus sacrario
tantum hoc venerandae (nisi forte fallor) vetustatis
 <COL N="0874C"></COL> monimentum collocatur.</HI></P> <P COM="0874"><HI REND="ITALIC">Et si vero nulli melius quam vos ipsi quae sit huic
exemplari fides habenda aestimarint, hac de re tamen
vos admonendos duxi, tantam a me in Lucae praesertim
Evangelio repertam esse inter hunc codicem et caeteros
quantumvis veteres discrepantiam, ut vitandae
quorumdam offensioni asservandum potius quam publicandum
existimem. In hac tamen non sententiarum,
sed vocum diversitate nihil profecto comperi, unde
suspicari potuerim a veteribus illis haereticis fuisse depravatum.
Imo multa mihi videor deprehendisse observatione
digna; quaedam etiam sic a recepta Scriptura
discrepantia, ut tamen cum veterum quorumdam,
et Graecorum, et Latinorum Patrum scriptis consentiant:
non pauca denique, quibus vetusta Latina editio
 <COL N="0874D"></COL> corroboratur: quae omnia pro ingenii mei modulo inter
se comparata, et cum Syra et Arabica editione collata,
in majores meas adnotationes a me super emendatas,
et brevi prodituras congessi.</HI></P> <P COM="0874"><HI REND="ITALIC">Sed age, res haec tota vestri, sicuti par est, judicii
esto. Tantum a vobis peto, ut hoc qualecumque summae
in vestram Amplitudinem observantiae meae veluti monimentum
 <COL N="0875A"></COL> ab homine vestri studiosissimo profectum,
aequi bonique consulatis,</HI>  etc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0875"><HI REND="ITALIC">Genevae,</HI>  VIII  <HI REND="ITALIC">Idus Decembris, anno Domini</HI>  CICICLXXXI,</CAPTION> <CAPTION COM="0875"><HI REND="ITALIC">Vestrae totius inclytae Academiae dignitati
addictissimus</HI> Theodorus Beza.</CAPTION> <CAPTION COM="0875">NOTA MANU THEODORI BEZAE CODICI INSCRIPTA.</CAPTION> <COL N="0876A"></COL> <P COM="0876"><HI REND="ITALIC">Est hoc exemplar venerandae vetustatis, ex Graecia,
ut apparet ex barbaris Graecis quibusdam notis ad marginem
ascriptis, olim exportatum, et in Sancti Irenaei
monasterio Lugduni, ita ut hic cernitur, mutilatum,
postquam ibi diu in pulvere jacuisset, repertum, oriente
ibi civili bello, anno Domini</HI>  1562.</P></DOC> <DOC NAME="Concordantes lectiones cum textu Graeco" AUTHOR="Auctor incertus" STATUS=S TEMPSTAT=UNCERT SECOND=YES COM="0876"><COL N="0875"></COL> <HEAD TYPE=main COM="0875">CONCORDANTES LECTIONES
EVANGELIARII QUADRUPLICIS
CUM TEXTU GRAECO,
IN LOCIS ABEUNTIBUS AB EDITIONE VULGATA.</HEAD> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0875"><HEAD COM="0875">S. MATTHAEUS.</HEAD> <COL N="0875B"></COL> <CAPTION COM="0875">CAP. I.</CAPTION> <P COM="0875">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Esron.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Esrwvm.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Veron.
et Corbeien.</P> <CAPTION COM="0875">CAP. II.</CAPTION> <P COM="0875">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Bethlehem Juda.</HI>  In Graeco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðû
1Ioudaivaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Judaeae.</HI>  Et ita in Vercell., San-Ger., Veron.,
Brix. Alteram Bethlehem, quae in tribu Zabulon,
Josue XIX, 15, tum in Hebraeo exemplari,
tum in Latino vulgato collocatur, cur libri Graeci expunxerunt,
et pro Bethlehem,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Baiqmoún</FOREIGN>  scripserunt?
At haec altera,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bethlehem Juda</HI>  appellatur etiam Judic.
XIX, 1.</P> <P COM="0875">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ubi Christus nasceretur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gennaðtai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi
Christus nascitur.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et San-Ger.</P> <P COM="0875">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Bethlehem Judae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðû 1Ioudaivaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Judaeae,</HI> 
ut versu 1. Et ita Verc., Brix.</P> <P COM="0875">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Diligenter didicit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hjkrivbwse,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">exquisivit.</HI> 
Et ita Verc. et San-Ger. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0875">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Interrogate.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxetavsate.</FOREIGN>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">requirite
diligenter.</HI></P> <P COM="0875"><COL N="0875C"></COL> 11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et intrantes domum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejlqovnteû eijû
thún oijkivan,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et venientes in domum.</HI>  Verc. quoque, Veron.
et Brix. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in domum.</HI></P> <P COM="0875">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui consurgens.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ deú ejgerqeiúû.</FOREIGN>  Et sic
iterum versu 21. Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ille autem surgens.</HI>  Verc. et
Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">surgens autem;</HI>  et ita San-Ger.</P> <CAPTION COM="0875">CAP. III.</CAPTION> <P COM="0875">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">A ventura ira.</HI>  In Graeco hic est:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoú thðû mellouvshû ojrghðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">a futura ira.</HI>  Et ita in Corb.,
Veron.</P> <P COM="0875">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fructum dignum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>karpouúû ajxivouû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fructus
dignos,</HI>  ut apud Lucam. Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0875">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui post me venturus est.</HI>  Graece est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ ejrcovmenoû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">qui venit.</HI>  Verc. habet:  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui autem venit.</HI></P> <P COM="0875">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ego a te debeo.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgwú creivan eæcw,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ego
opus habeo.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0875">CAP. IV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0875">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vade, Satana.</HI>  In Graecis multis
mss. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåpage ojpivsw mou, Satanað.</FOREIGN>  In Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Vade retro me, Satanas.</HI>  At Verc. et Corb. habent,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Vade retro, Satanas.</HI></P> <P COM="0875">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Prophetam.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>levgontoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dicentem.</HI> 
 <COL N="0875D"></COL> Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0875">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et patre.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">suo.</HI>  Et ita
in San-Ger. et in Veron.</P> <P COM="0875">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Opinio ejus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkohú aujtouð.</FOREIGN>  San-Ger. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">fama.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0875">CAP. V.</CAPTION> <P COM="0875">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Videns autem</HI>  JESUS  <HI REND="ITALIC">turbas.</HI>  Non est
in Graeco nomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesus.</HI>  Nec habetur in Brix. et Ver.</P> <P COM="0875">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Possidebunt terram.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>klhronomhvsousi.</FOREIGN> 
Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">haereditabunt.</HI>  Et Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">haereditate possidebunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0875">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui irascitur.</HI>  Graece additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijkhð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sine causa.</HI> 
Et ita Verc., Veron., Corb., Brix. Prave, tametsi
hanc vocem habent omnes mss. Graeci, etiam Cantabrigiensis,
uno excepto codice Vaticano.</P> <P COM="0875">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et vade prius reconciliari.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú uåpage,
prwðton diallavghqi twðé ajdelfwðé sou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et abi, prius reconciliare
fratri tuo.</HI>  Verc., Veron. et Brix. habent:  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
vade, prius reconciliare fratri tuo.</HI></P> <P COM="0875">41.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Alia duo.</HI>  Non est in Graeco vox,  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia.</HI>  Nec in
Brix.</P> <P COM="0875"><COL N="0876B"></COL> 44.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Benefacite his, qui oderunt vos.</HI>  His verbis
Graeci codices praeponunt ista:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujlogeiðte touúû katarwmevnouû
uJmaðû.</FOREIGN>  Brix. quoque,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Benedicite maledicentibus
vos.</HI></P> <P COM="0876">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pro persequentibus, et calumniantibus vos.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpeúr twðn ejphreazovntwn uJmaðû, kaiú diwkovntwn.</FOREIGN> 
Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro calumniantibus vobis, et persequentibus
vos.</HI>  Verc. quoque et Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro calumniantibus,
et persequentibus vos.</HI></P> <P COM="0876">46.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quam mercedem habebitis?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæcete,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">habetis.</HI> 
Et ita Corb.</P> <P COM="0876">48.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Coelestis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ ejn toiðû oujranoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui in coelis
est.</HI>  Et ita Veron. et San-Ger.</P> <CAPTION COM="0876">CAP. VI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0876">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Justitiam vestram.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thún ejlehmosuvnhn
uJmwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">eleemosynam vestram,</HI>  cum Brix.</P> <P COM="0876">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Reddet tibi</HI>  (Nam  <HI REND="ITALIC">beati misericordes, quoniam
ipsi misericordiam consequentur</HI> ). Graeci codices, tum
in hoc versu, tum in versu 6 et 18, addunt,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0876C"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>fanerwðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in manifesto:</HI>  et ita Brix. Verc. quoque et
San-Ger. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in palam.</HI>  Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in pala.</HI></P> <P COM="0876">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adveniat.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejlqevtw,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">veniat.</HI>  Et ita Corb.</P> <P COM="0876">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Amen.</HI>  Hic Graeci codices addunt:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti sou ejstiún
hJ basileiva, kaiú hJ duvnamiû, kaiú hJ dovxa eijû touúû aijwðnaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quia
tuum est regnum, et tua est potestas, et gloria in saecula.</HI> 
Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quoniam tuum est regnum, et virtus,
et gloria in saecula.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0876">CAP. VII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0876">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Excidetur, et in ignem mittetur.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkkovptetai, kaiú eijû puðr bavlletai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">exciditur, et
in ignem mittitur,</HI>  ut Matth. III, 10. Verc. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">exciditur,
et in ignem mittetur,</HI>  sumpto  <HI REND="ITALIC">e,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">i,</HI>  ut etiam
Corb.  <HI REND="ITALIC">excidetur, et in ignem mittitur.</HI></P> <P COM="0876">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ipse intrabit in regnum coelorum.</HI>  Et ita Brix.
Non sunt haec verba in Graecis codicibus.</P> <P COM="0876">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eorum et Pharisaei.</HI>  Desunt haec verba in Graecis
codicibus. In Brix. quoque deest,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Pharisaei.</HI> 
Pharisaei, ut ego opinor, ne praeter Scribas, populum
ex officio docuisse existimentur, fuerunt in
 <COL N="0876D"></COL> nonnullis Codd. omissi.</P> <CAPTION COM="0876">CAP. VIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0876">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ego veniam, et curabo eum.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Egwú ejlqwðn qerapeuvsw ajutoún.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Verc., Brix. et
San-Ger.</P> <P COM="0876">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In illa hora.</HI>  Mss. Graeci decem et amplius hic
addunt ista:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú uJpostrevyaû oJ eJkatovntarcoû eijû thún oiøkon
auJtouð, ejn aujthðé thðé wåraé eußre toún paiðda auJtouð uJgiaivnonta</FOREIGN> ;
et ita San-Ger.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex illa hora.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0876">CAP. IX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0876">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Remittuntur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajfevwntai.</FOREIGN>  Et ita
Verc., Veron., San-Ger. in praeterito Attico, pro
communi  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajfeiðntai</FOREIGN>  In praesenti est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajfiventai.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0876">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ait.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiøpen aujtoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ait illis.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0876">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed peccatores.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû metavnoian,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ad poenitentiam.</HI>  Et ita in San-Ger. ex Luca,
apud quem legitur, cap. V, vers. 32. Non est hic in
mss. Cantabrigiensi.</P> <P COM="0876">32.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mutum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kwfoún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">surdum.</HI>  Verc., Veron.,
San Ger. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">mutum et surdum.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0876">CAP. X.</CAPTION> <P COM="0876">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et Thaddaeus.</HI>  In Graeco hic legitur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú Lebbaivoû oJ ejpiklhqeiúû Qaddaiðoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et Lebbaeus, qui
 <COL N="0877A"></COL> cognominatus est Thaddaeus.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Lebbeus,
qui nominatur Taddaeus.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In civitates.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû povlin,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in civitatem.</HI>  Et
ita Corb.</P> <P COM="0877">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mortuos suscitate.</HI>  Graeci quidam codices mss.
et Brix. haec verba non habent. Quidam etiam ista
omittunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">daemones ejicite;</HI>  qui vero utrumque habent,
istud  <HI REND="ITALIC">leprosos mundate</HI>  huic dicto praeponunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">mortuos
suscitate.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae audistis et vidistis.</HI>  Quaeque
narrantur strictim a Luca, cap. VII, vers 21. Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkouvete kaiú blevpete,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">auditis et videtis.</HI>  Et ita Veron.;
Verc. vero habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">audistis et videtis.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ante faciem tuam.</HI>  Apud Malachiam legitur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ante faciem meam,</HI>  et ita in Verc. Sed nihil interest,
cum Christus sit Deus ipse Altissimus et Dominus:
juxta illud de eodem Joanne Baptista. Luc. I, 76:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Et tu, puer, Propheta Altissimi vocaberis: praeibis
enim</HI>  ANTE FACIEM DOMINI  <HI REND="ITALIC">parare vias ejus.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fuit placitum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgevneto eujdokiva,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fuit beneplacitum.</HI> 
 <COL N="0877B"></COL> Et ita San-Ger. et Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XII. 1.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sabbato.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toiðû savbbasi,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sabbatis.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Corb., San-Ger., Veron. et
Brix.</P> <P COM="0877">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mutus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kwfoúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">surdus.</HI>  Veron. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">mutus et surdus.</HI>  Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">surdus et mutus.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non remittetur.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toiðû ajnqrwvpoiû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hominibus.</HI>  Et ita in Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Volucres coeli.</HI>  In Graeco vulgato
deest vox illa,  <HI REND="ITALIC">coeli.</HI>  Et ita in Corb. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0877">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Creverunt spinae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnevbhsan,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ascenderunt.</HI> 
Et ita Corb. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0877">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vis, imus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qevleiû ouøn ajpelqovnteû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vis igitur
ut abeuntes,</HI>  etc. Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vis ergo, abeuntes.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad comburendum.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtaú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ea.</HI> 
Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0877">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Filii nequam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ uiJoiú touð ponhrouð.</FOREIGN>  Veron.
legit  <HI REND="ITALIC">filii iniqui;</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">filii maligni,</HI>  hoc est,
diaboli. Propterea in Latina editione,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nequam,</HI>  est
 <COL N="0877C"></COL> in secundo casu.</P> <P COM="0877">51.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Etiam.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>naiú, Kuvrie,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">etiam, Domine.</HI> 
Verc., Veron., Brix., San-Ger. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">utique, Domine.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XIV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mergi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katapontivzesqai,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">demergi, submergi.</HI>  Corb. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Demergere.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Me honorat.</HI>  Textus Graecus habet,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejggivzei moi oJ laoúû oußtoû twðé stovmati aujtwðn, kaiú toiðû ceivlesiv
me timaðé.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">appropinquat se mihi populus hic ore
suo, et labiis suis me honorat.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Turbis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toún oæclon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">turbae.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">turbam.</HI></P> <P COM="0877">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mutos.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kwfouúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">surdos.</HI>  Et ita Corb.</P> <P COM="0877">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mutos loquentes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kwfouúû lalouðntaû,
kullouúû, uJgieiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">surdos loquentes, debiles sanos.</HI>  Brixian.
habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">mutos loquentes, debiles sanos.</HI>  Debiles
sanos idcirco omisisse Matthaeus videtur, quod existimarit
minora ex majoribus miraculis satis intelligi.</P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XVI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rogaverunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejphrwvthsan,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">interrogaverunt.</HI>  Et ita Corb.</P> <P COM="0877"><COL N="0877D"></COL> 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Faciem.</HI>  In Graeco praemittitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Upokritaiú.</FOREIGN>  Et
ita in Corb. et Brix. quod editio Latina non habet.</P> <P COM="0877">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Trans fretam.</HI>  Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">trans erat.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû toú
pevran.</FOREIGN>  Sic libri Graeci semper. Nam quater apud
Matthaeum illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">trans fretum,</HI>  scripserunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû toú pevran</FOREIGN> ;
et apud Marcum quater similiter, cap. V, vers.
1, 21, VI, 45 et VIII, 13.</P> <P COM="0877">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quem dicunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tivna me levgousin,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quem me
dicunt.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Veron., Corb., Brix. et San-Germ.</P> <P COM="0877">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Absit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iålewvû soi.</FOREIGN>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">propitius
esto tibi.</HI>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">propitius tibi.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">absit a te, propitius
esto.</HI>  Syrus Interpres.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Parce tibi:</HI>   <ORNAMENT IMAGE="0120877A" TEXT="[Hebrew Text]"></ORNAMENT></P> <CAPTION COM="0877">CAP. XVII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0877">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Venturus est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eærcetai
prwðton,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">venit primum.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Veniet primum.</HI> 
Matth. XI, 14, Christus Dominus de Joanne Baptista,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ipse est Elias,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui venturus est:</HI>  hoc est, qui
praedictus est esse venturus.</P> <P COM="0877"><COL N="0878A"></COL> 20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Per orationem et jejunium.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn proseuchðé
kaiú nhsteivaé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in oratione et jejunio.</HI>  Et ita Brix. ex
Marc. IX, 28.</P> <P COM="0878">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Conversantibus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnastrefomevnoiû.</FOREIGN>  Corb.
habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">redeuntibus.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0878">CAP. XVIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0878">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">De cordibus vestris.</HI>  Hic addunt
Graeci codices,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú paraptwvmata aujtwðn,</FOREIGN>  cum Brix.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">peccata eorum.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0878">CAP. XIX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0878">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui fecit hominem ab initio.</HI>  Graece
tantum,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ poihvsaû ajp1 ajrchðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui fecit ab initio.</HI>  Et
ita Verc. et San-Ger.</P> <P COM="0878">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et dimittere.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujthún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">eam.</HI>  Et
ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0878">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">De matris utero.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk koilivaû mhtroúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ex
alvo matris.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex utero matris.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid me interrogas de bono?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tiv me levgeiû
ajgaqoún</FOREIGN> ;  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid me dicis bonum?</HI>  Et ita Brix. ut apud
Lucam.</P> <P COM="0878">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae habes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>souð taú uJpavrconta.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">bona tua.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0878">CAP. XX.</CAPTION> <COL N="0878B"></COL> <P COM="0878">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Simile est.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gaúr</FOREIGN>  additur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">simile
est enim.</HI>  Et ita habent Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0878">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ite et vos in vineam meam.</HI>  Addunt hic libri Graeci:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú oå ejaún hø divkaion, lhvyeste,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et quod fuerit justum
accipietis.</HI>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et quod justum est accipietis.</HI>  In solo
ms. Cantabrig. ea non leguntur.</P> <P COM="0878">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Annon licet mihi quod volo facere?</HI>  Addunt libri
Graeci,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn toiúû ejmoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">de meo, in rebus meis.</HI>  Et
ita videtur legisse Vercell.</P> <P COM="0878">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quem ego bibiturus sum.</HI>  Addunt hic libri Graeci:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú toú bavptisma, oÝ ejgwú baptivzomai, baptisqhðnai,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et baptismo, quo ego baptizor, baptizari?</HI>  et versu sequenti
similia: quae sunt huc ex Marco translata:
nisi quod pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">aut,</HI>  habent  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et.</HI>  Brix. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">aut
baptisma baptizari, quo ego.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Calicem quidem meum bibetis.</HI>  Post  <HI REND="ITALIC">bibetis,</HI>  in
textu Graeco legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú toú bavptisma, oÝ ejgwú baptivzomai
baptisqhvsesqe.</FOREIGN>  Cui lectioni fere consonat Brix.
habens,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et baptisma, quo ego baptizor, baptizamini.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0878">CAP. XXI.</CAPTION> <COL N="0878C"></COL> <P COM="0878">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Populi autem.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ deú oæcloi
eælegon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">turbae autem dicebant.</HI>  Et ita Brix. et Corb.
In ms. Cantabrig. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ deú polloiú eiøpon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">multi
vero dixerunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ibique mansit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú kulivsqh ejkeið.</FOREIGN>  Brix.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et requievit illic.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tolle.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aærqhti,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tollere.</HI>  Et ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0878">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Omnes enim habebant Joannem sicut prophetam.</HI> 
Scriptum est in Graeco  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæcousi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">habent.</HI>  Et ita
Veron. et San-Ger.</P> <P COM="0878">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dicunt ei: Primus.</HI>  In ms. Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæscatoû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">novissimus.</HI>  Et ita in Verc., Corb., San-Germ. et
Veron.</P> <P COM="0878">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et habebimus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú katavscwmen.</FOREIGN>  Corb.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et possideamus.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0878">CAP. XXII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0878">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In villam suam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû toún
iædion ajgroún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in suum agrum.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ad agrum
suum.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rex autem.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ basileuúû ejkeiðnoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">rex ille.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.; Veron. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ille rex.</HI></P> <P COM="0878"><COL N="0878D"></COL> 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Discumbentium.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnakeimevnwn.</FOREIGN>  Corb. legit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">recumbentium.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Erunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijsiún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sunt.</HI>  Et ita Corb., Veron.
et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0878">CAP. XXIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0878">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fimbrias.</HI>  In Graeco additur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>twðn iJmativwn aujtwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vestimentorum suorum.</HI>  Et ita in
Brix.</P> <P COM="0878">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Orationes longas orantes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú profavsei
makraúé proseucovmenoi.</FOREIGN>  Veron. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">occasione longa
orantes.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sub obtentu prolixae orationis.</HI>  Versus
hic 14 integer deest in quibusdam Latinis.</P> <P COM="0878">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et immunditia.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ajkrasivaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et intemperantia.</HI> 
Et ita Verc. In aliis quibusdam,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ajdikivaû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et injustitia.</HI>  Et ita in Brix. Sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">immunditiam</HI>  legi oportere,
constat ex versu sequenti, ubi habetur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Munda
prius quod intus est.</HI></P> <P COM="0878">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui effusus est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkcunovmenon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui effunditur.</HI> 
Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0878"><COL N="0879A"></COL> 37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et noluisti.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú oujk hjqelhvsate,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et noluistis.</HI> 
Et ita Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. XXIV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec fieri.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnta genevsqai,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">omnia fieri.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tunicam suam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú iJmavtia aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vestimenta
sua.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum virtute multa et majestate.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>metaú
dunavmewû kaiú dovxhû pollhðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cum virtute et gloria multa.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">36.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nisi solus pater.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij mhú oJ pathvr mou
movnoû.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi Pater meus solus.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. XXV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quinque autem ex eis erant fatuae,
et quinque prudentes.</HI>  In Graeco e contrario prudentes
fatuis praeponuntur, ut in Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum lampadibus.</HI>  Graece additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">suis.</HI>  Et
ita in Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Novissime vero.</HI>  In Graeco est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåsteron,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">postea,</HI>  ut
in Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et omnes angeli.</HI>  Graece,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú pavnteû oiJ aågioi
aæggeloi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et omnes sancti angeli.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. XXVI.</CAPTION> <COL N="0879B"></COL> <P COM="0879">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tradetur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paradivdotai,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">traditur.</HI>  Et ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0879">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Effundetur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkcunovmenon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui effunditur.</HI> 
Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0879">59.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Morti traderent.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qanatwvswsi,</FOREIGN>  Verc.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">interficerent.</HI></P> <P COM="0879">60.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Novissime.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåsteron,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">postea.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0879">61.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et post triduum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú diaú triwðn hJmerwðn.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et in tribus diebus, et per triduum.</HI></P> <P COM="0879">65.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Blasphemiam.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ejus.</HI> 
Et ita in Veron. et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. XXVII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Habebat autem.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiøcon,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">habebant.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Veron. et Brix, ut ad Judaeos
referatur, non ad praesidem.</P> <P COM="0879">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dicunt omnes.</HI>  In Graeco: inseritur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dicunt
ei omnes.</HI>  Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tradidit eis.</HI>  Graeci libri non habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">eis,</HI> 
excepto Cantabrig. Deest etiam in Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. XXVIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ecce praedixi vobis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijdouú</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0879C"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiøpon uJmiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ecce dixi vobis.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Corb. et
Veron.</P> <P COM="0879">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Discipulis ejus.</HI>  Hic libri Graeci addunt:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû dev
ejporeuvonto ajpaggeiðlai toiðû maqhtaiðû aujtouð.</FOREIGN>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut
autem abierunt nuntiare discipulis ejus.</HI></P> <P COM="0879">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Usque ad consummationem saeculi.</HI>  In Graeco
additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajmhvn.</FOREIGN>  Et ita in Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0879"><HEAD COM="0879">S. JOANNES.</HEAD> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. I.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">4. In  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipso vita erat.</HI>  In Cantabrig. codice
Graeco sic legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn aujtwðé zwhv ejstin×</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in ipso vita est.</HI> 
Et ita in Corb. et Brix. Verc. quoque, Gat. et mss.
legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in illo vita est.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in eo vita est.</HI></P> <P COM="0879">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joannes testimonium perhibet de ipso, et clamat.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>martureið</FOREIGN>  (Verc. et Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">testificatur</HI> )
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periú aujtouð, kaiú kevkrage.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0879">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ipse est qui post me venturus est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtovû
ejstin oJ ojpivsw mou ejrcovmenoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui post me venit.</HI>  Et ita
Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">43.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In crastinum voluit exire.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðé ejpauvrion,</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0879D"></COL> ut versu 29 et 35, ubi Latine legitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">altera die.</HI>  Et
ita Verc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. II.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et dicit ei</HI>  JESUS. Graece,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>levgei aujthðé,</FOREIGN> 
absque conjunctione  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú,</FOREIGN>  quae deest etiam in Verc.,
sed in Alexandrino legitur.</P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. III.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nisi quis renatus fuerit denuo.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejaún mhv tiû gennhqhðé aænwqen,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi quis natus fuerit
de sursum.</HI>  Brix. habet:  <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi quis natus fuerit denuo.</HI> 
Gat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi qui natus fuerit.</HI></P> <P COM="0879">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Facta est autem quaestio.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgevneto ouøn,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">facta est igitur.</HI>  Verc. Et Brix. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">facta est ergo.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0879">CAP. IV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0879">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut ergo cognovit</HI>  JESUS. Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû ouøn eægnw oJ Kuvrioû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut ergo cognovit Dominus.</HI>  Et
ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0879">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quamquam</HI>  JESUS  <HI REND="ITALIC">non baptizaret.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ihsouúû
aujtoúû,</FOREIGN>  JESUS  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipse.</HI>  Et ita in Verc., Veron. et Brix.
Gat. et Mm. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipse Jesus.</HI></P> <P COM="0879">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Reliquit Judaeam,</HI>  Cantabrigiensis codex habet,
 <COL N="0880A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Ioudaivan ghðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Judaeam terram:</HI>  et ita Veron., Gat. et
Mm.; Verc. quoque,  <HI REND="ITALIC">terram Judaeam.</HI></P> <P COM="0880">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et dicit illis hominibus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú levgei toiðû
ajnqrwvpoiû,</FOREIGN>  sine pronomine,  <HI REND="ITALIC">illis.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Veron.
et Corb. Alius codex Graecus habet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>polivtaiû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">civibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0880">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Interea rogabant eum discipuli.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn deú
twðé metaxuú hjrwvtwn aujtoún oiJ maqhtaiv.</FOREIGN>  Vox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejrwtaðén.</FOREIGN>  non
 <HI REND="ITALIC">rogare,</HI>  sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">interrogare</HI>  sonat, ut habet Verc. Attamen
in libris Graecis Novi ac Veteris Testamenti,
praesertim vero apud Evangelistas, vox illa occurrit,
ubicumque fere in Latino  <HI REND="ITALIC">rogare</HI>  est.</P> <P COM="0880">40.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rogaverunt eum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hjrwvtwn aujtoún.</FOREIGN>  Et
ita Verc. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0880">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non propter tuam loquelam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujk eæti diaú
thún shún laliavn.</FOREIGN>  Cantabrigiensis,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>marturivan,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non propter
tuum testimonium.</HI>  Et ita Veron. Antiquo interpreti
visa vox est  <HI REND="ITALIC">testimonii,</HI>  quam  <HI REND="ITALIC">loquelae</HI>  dignior.</P> <P COM="0880">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quia hic est vere Salvator mundi.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ swthúr touð kovsmou oJ Cristoúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Salvator mundi Christus.</HI> 
Et ita Brix. necnon Syrus interpres ex Graeco.</P> <P COM="0880"><COL N="0880B"></COL> 46.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et erat quidam regulus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú høn tiû
basilikoúû.</FOREIGN>  Verc. legit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Basiliscus;</HI>  quia forte. Latinus
interpres legit inconsiderate  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basilivskoû,</FOREIGN>  pro eo quod
scriptum erat Graece,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basilikovû.</FOREIGN> .</P> <P COM="0880">47.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Incipiebat enim mori.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hæmelle gaúr ajpoqnhvskein.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">erat enim moriturus.</HI></P> <P COM="0880">49.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Filius meus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toú paidivon mou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">puer meus.</HI> 
Veron. et Corb. habent tantum  <HI REND="ITALIC">puer.</HI>  In Alexandrino
est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toún uiJovn mou.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0880">51.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quia filius ejus viveret.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti oJ paiðû sou zhðé.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. et Veron. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quoniam filius tuus vivit.</HI> 
Cantabrigiensis,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ uiJovû.</FOREIGN></P> <CAPTION COM="0880">CAP. V.</CAPTION> <P COM="0880">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Est autem Hierosolymis probatica
piscina.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæsti deú ejn toiðû 2Ierosoluvmoiû ejpiú thðé
probatikhðé kolumbhvqraé.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">est autem in Jerosolymis
super Probatica piscina.</HI>  Gat. quoque et Mm. habent, . . .
 <HI REND="ITALIC">super Probatica.</HI></P> <P COM="0880">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bethsaïda.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beqesdav.</FOREIGN>  Atque ita Brix. et
Syrus interpres ex Graeco. In versione Coptica retenta
 <COL N="0880C"></COL> vox est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beqsaiçdav.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0880">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aridorum.</HI>  Cantabrigiensis codex addit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paralutikwðn.</FOREIGN> 
Et ita Verc. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0880">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Angelus autem Domini.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæggeloû gaúr,</FOREIGN> 
omisso nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domini,</HI>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gaúr</FOREIGN>  posito, pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dev.</FOREIGN>  Et
ita Veron., Corb. et Gat., qui tamen pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">autem,</HI> 
habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">enim.</HI>  In Graeco Bezae codice, quem dicunt
esse vetustissimum, quartus hic versus plane omittitur.
In Alexandrino legitur vox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kurivou.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0880">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Descendebat in piscinam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katevbainen ejn thðé
kolumbhvqraé.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">descendebat in natatoria.</HI>  Et ita
Veronensis. In Alexandrino codice,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejlouveto,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">lavabatur.</HI></P> <P COM="0880">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et movebatur aqua.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejtavrasse toú
uådwr,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et turbabat aquam,</HI>  angelus nimirum. Et ita
Verc., Corb., Veron., Gat. et mss.</P> <P COM="0880">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Propterea persequebantur Judaei</HI>  JESUM. Addunt
Graeci codices:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejzhvtoun aujtoún ajpokteiðnai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et quaerebant
eum interficere.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0880">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et potestatem dedit et judicium facere.</HI>  Graece:
 <COL N="0880D"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú krivsin poieiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et judicium facere.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
judicium faciendi.</HI></P> <P COM="0880">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Audient vocem Filii Dei.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkouvsontai
thðû fwnhðû aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">audient vocem ejus.</HI>  Et ita Verc.,
Gat., mss., Veron. et Brix. Codices Graeci tres, vel
plures, versu 25 tantum legunt,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkouvsontai thðû fwnhðû
touð Qeouð,</FOREIGN>  non, ut alii habent,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð UiJouð touð Qeouð.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0880">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed voluntatem ejus, qui misit me.</HI>  Graecus
addit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>patrovû.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Veron. ac Brix.</P> <P COM="0880">46.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Crederetis forsitan et mihi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpisteuvete
aÞn ejmoiú.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">crederetis et mihi.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0880">CAP. VI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0880">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Trans mare Galilaeae, quod est Tiberiadis.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pevraû thðû qalavsshû thðû Galilaivaû thðû
Tiberiavdoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">trans mare Galilaeae Tiberiadis.</HI>  Et ita
Verc. In Cantabrigiensi,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû taú mevrh thðû Tiberiavdoû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">in partes Tiberiadis,</HI>  ut in Veron.</P> <P COM="0880">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Accepit ergo </HI>  JESUS  <HI REND="ITALIC">panes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eælabe deú,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">accepit autem.</HI>  Et ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0880"><COL N="0881A"></COL> 11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Distribuit discumbentibus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>devdwke toiðû
maqhtaiðû, oiJ deú maqhtaiú toiðû ajnakeimevnoiû.</FOREIGN>  Veron.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et dedit discipulis suis, discipuli autem discumbentibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ne pereant.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna mhv ti ajpovlhtai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ne
quid pereat.</HI>  Et ita Verc.; Brix. quoque, et Veron.
legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ne quid ex illis pereat.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fugit iterum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnecwvrhse pavlin,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">secessit
iterum.</HI>  Et ita Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0881">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quia navicula alia non erat ibi, nisi una.</HI>  Graece
legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij mhú eån ejkeiðno eijû oÝ ajnevbhsan oiJ maqhtaiú aujtouð.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi una, in qua ascenderant discipuli
Jesu.</HI>  In Cantabrig. quoque ms. legitur . . .  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>maqhtaiú
1Ihsouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">discipuli Jesu.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aliae vero supervenerunt naves.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aælla
deú hølqe ploiavria,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aliae vero venerunt naves.</HI>  Et ita Verc.
et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">aliae vero naves venerunt.</HI>  Cantabrigiensis
codex Graecus habet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aællwn ploiarivwn ejlqovntwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aliis
navigiis venientibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ascenderunt in naviculas.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnevbhsan kaiú</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0881B"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoiú eijû taú ploiða,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ingressi sunt et ipsi in navigia.</HI>  In
Cantabrig. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eælabon eJautoiðû ploiavria.</FOREIGN>  In Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">acceperunt sibi ipsi naviculas.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non quia vidistis signa.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>shmeiða.</FOREIGN>  Cantabrigiensis
addit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú tevrata,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et prodigia.</HI>  Et ita Verc.,
Gat., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0881"><HI REND="ITALIC">Et vidistis me, et non creditis.</HI>  Alexandrinus codex
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eJwravkate, kaiú ouj pisteuvete.</FOREIGN>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et vidistis, sed
non creditis.</HI>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et videtis, et non creditis.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non ejiciam foras.</HI>  Cantabrigiensis codex non
habet illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">foras,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæxw</FOREIGN> ; uti nec Verc. aut Veron.</P> <P COM="0881">45.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Omnis, qui audivit a Patre.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Paðû ouøn oJ
ajkouvsaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">omnis igitur qui audivit.</HI>  At in alio,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkouvwn,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">qui audit;</HI>  ut habent Verc., Veron. et Gat.</P> <P COM="0881">52.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et panis, quem ego dabo, caro mea est pro
mundi vita.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú aærtoû deú oÝn ejgwú dwvsw, hJ savrx
mou ejstin, hÝn ejgwú dwvsw uJpeúr thðû touð kovsmou zwhðû.</FOREIGN> 
Brix. legit sic,  <HI REND="ITALIC">panis enim hic, quem ego dabo, caro
mea est, quam ego dabo pro hujus mundi vita.</HI></P> <P COM="0881"><COL N="0881C"></COL> 56.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vere est cibus . . . . vere est potus.</HI>  Unus e mss.
Stephani non habet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajlhqwðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vere,</HI>  sed utrobique  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajlhqhúû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">verus:</HI>  et ita mss. ut Leontius, et Appollinaris
in Catena.</P> <P COM="0881">57.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ego in illo.</HI>  Addit ms. Cantabrigiensis:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejaún mhú
lavbhte toú swðma touð uiJouð touð ajnqrwvpou, wJû toún aærton thðû
zwhðû, oujk eæcete zwhún ejn aujtwðé.</FOREIGN>  In Verc. et Corb. legitur
ita:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si acceperit homo corpus Filii hominis, quemadmodum
panem vitae, habebit vitam in eo.</HI>  At in
Corb. pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">in eo,</HI>  est  <HI REND="ITALIC">in illo.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">60.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Capharnaum.</HI>  Addit Cantabrigiensis ms. et
alter Stephani,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sabbavtwé.</FOREIGN>  Et quidam scriptores Latini
legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">docens sabbato in Capharnaum,</HI>  ut Verc. et
Corb.</P> <P COM="0881">70.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quia tu es Christus, Filius Dei.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð
Qeouð touð zwðntoû.</FOREIGN>  Corb. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dei vivi.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0881">CAP. VII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0881">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vos, ascendite ad diem festum hunc.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû thún eJorthún tauvthn.</FOREIGN>  Sed exemplaria quaedam
omittunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tauthún,</FOREIGN>  sicut Verc. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0881">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ego autem non ascendo ad diem festum istum.</HI> 
 <COL N="0881D"></COL> Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgwú ouæpw ajnabaivnw eijû thún eJorthún tauvthn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ego
nondum ascendo ad diem festum istum.</HI>  Brix. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ego autem nondum ascendo ad diem festum hunc.</HI>  Sic
innumeri pene codices Graeci, maxime vero antiquissimus
ille Vaticanus toto terrarum orbe celeberrimus.</P> <P COM="0881">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec cum dixisset, ipse mansit in Galilaea.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tauðta deú eijpwðn aujtoiðû</FOREIGN>  (Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec dicens
illis.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec autem dixit eis.</HI>  Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec cum
dixisset illis</HI> ),  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæmeinen ejn thðé Galilaivaé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">haec autem cum
dixisset ispis, mansit in Galilaea.</HI></P> <P COM="0881">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nemo tamen palam loquebatur de illo.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujdeiúû mevn toi parjrJhsivaé.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nemo tamen fiducialiter,</HI> 
etc.</P> <P COM="0881">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Numquid vere cognoverunt principes, quia hic
est Christus?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Mhvpote ajlhqwðû eægnwsan oiJ aærconteû
oåti oußtovû ejstin ajlhqwðû oJ Cristoúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">numquid vere
cognoverunt principes, quia hic est vere Christus?</HI>  Et
 <COL N="0882A"></COL> ita Brix. Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">numquid forte vere cognoverunt . . . . .</HI> 
Sic versu 41, quidam mss. Graeci habent,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oußtovû ejstin
ajlhqwðû oJ Cristoúû.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hic est vere Christus:</HI>  ubi Latina
editio,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hic est Christus</HI>  tantum.</P> <P COM="0882">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gentium . . Gentes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ellhvnwn</FOREIGN>  et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>4Ellhnaû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Graecorum, et Graecos.</HI>  Et ita Vere. Corb. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0882">52.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Numquid et tu Galilaeus es?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhú kaiú
suú ejk thðû Galilaivaû eiø,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non et tu ex Galilaea es?</HI>  Brix.
habet:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Numquid et tu a Galilaea es?</HI></P> <P COM="0882">52.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Scrutare Scripturas, et vide.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejreuvnhson,
kaiú iæde,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">scrutare et vide.</HI>  Et ita Gat, Mm. et Brix.
Tamen in Cantabrig. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejreuvnhson taúû Grafaúû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">scrutare Scripturas.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0882">CAP. VIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0882">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Digito scribebat in terra.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû
thún ghðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in terram.</HI>  Et ita Corb., Gat. et mss. Addunt
quidam mss. Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhú prospoiouvmenoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non simulans,
non fingens;</HI>  hoc est illos reipsa condemnans. Alii
e diverso,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú prospoiouvmenoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et hoc sibi sumens,</HI> 
nempe pro potestate. Nam ei verbo illa utraque significatio
convenit.</P> <P COM="0882"><COL N="0882B"></COL> 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et mulier in medio stans.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJstwðsa.</FOREIGN>  At
in Cantabrig. ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouøsa.</FOREIGN>  Corb. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">erat.</HI>  Alii Graeci
verbum illud prorsus omittunt.</P> <P COM="0882">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui sequitur me, non ambulat in tenebris.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj mhú peripathvsei ejn thðé skotivaé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non ambulabit
in tenebris.</HI>  Et ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0882">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Forsitan et Patrem meum sciretis.</HI>  Non dubitantis
haec particula  <HI REND="ITALIC">forsitan,</HI>  sed affirmantis est.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Forsitan</HI>  hoc loco idem sonat atque  <HI REND="ITALIC">utique,</HI>  ut legitur
in Vercell.; cui lectioni favent etiam Veron. et
Graeci codices, in quibus ea vox abest.</P> <P COM="0882">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Principium, qui et loquor vobis.</HI>  Obscurus hic
locus ut interpretibus videretur, fecit lectio Graeca,
quae est profecto perplexa. Est enim hujusmodi:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Thún ajrchún oå ti kaiú lalwð uJmiðn.</FOREIGN>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Principium,
quod et loquor vobis.</HI>  Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in primis, quia loquor
vobis.</HI>  Gat. et Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Principium, quod loquor.</HI></P> <P COM="0882">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et non cognoverunt quia Patrem ejus dicebat
Deum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti toún patevra aujtoiðû eælegen.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
 <COL N="0882C"></COL> legit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod Patrem illis diceret.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia de Patre
eis dicebat.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de . . . . Patre diceret eis.</HI>  Gat. et
Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Patrem eis . . . . dicebat.</HI>  Ut Latinus interpres
pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð, aujtoiðû</FOREIGN>  legerit. Ita etiam Syrus. In Cantabrig.
ms. habetur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti toún patevra aujtouð levgei toún Qeovn.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0882">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sicut docuit me Pater.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ pathvr mou,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Pater meus.</HI>  Et ita Brix. Sed non est illud  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mouð,</FOREIGN>  in
Cantabrig.</P> <P COM="0882">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et non reliquit me solum.</HI>  In Graeco additur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ pathvr.</FOREIGN>  Et ita in Brix. Sed non est ea vox in
Cantabrig.</P> <P COM="0882">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et vos quae vidistis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú uJmeiðû ouøn oÝ eJwravkate.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et vos itaque quod vidistis.</HI>  In Cantabrigiensi
ms. legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aÝ hjkouvsate,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quae audistis.</HI>  Et ita
in Brix.</P> <P COM="0882">39.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si filii Abrahae estis, opera Abrahae facite.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij tevkna touð 1Abraaúm høte, taú eærga touð
1Abraaúm ejpoieiðte aæn.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Si filii Abrahae essetis, opera
Abrahae faceretis.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0882">45.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ego autem si veritatem dico, non creditis mihi.</HI> 
 <COL N="0882D"></COL> Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgwú deú oåti thún ajlhvqeian levgw, ouj pisteuvetev moi.</FOREIGN> 
Gat. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ego autem quia veritatem . . . .</HI>  Verc., Veron.
et Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ego quia veritatem dico, non creditis mihi.</HI></P> <P COM="0882">49.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et vos inhonorastis me.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú uJmeiðû ajtimavzetev
me,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et vos inhonoratis me.</HI>  Et ita Corb. Verc.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non honorificatis.</HI>  Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">dehonorificatis.</HI></P> <P COM="0882">59.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et exivit de templo.</HI>  Graece additur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dielqwún
diaú mevsou aujtwðn, kaiú parhðgen ouåtwû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">transiens per medium
illorum; et sic praeteriit.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">transiens
per medium eorum, et ibat.</HI>  Quae verba non sunt in
ms. Cantabrig. sed habentur in Syro et Arabico.</P> <CAPTION COM="0882">CAP. IX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0882">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et praeteriens</HI>  JESUS. In Graeco non
est JESUS: nec in Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0882">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Discipuli ejus.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>levgonteû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dicentes.</HI> 
Et ita in Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0882">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Silae.</HI>  In Graeco est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Siloaúm,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Siloam.</HI>  Et ita in
Verc. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0882">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui viderant eum prius, quia mendieus erat.</HI> 
 <COL N="0883A"></COL> Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti tufloúû høn.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod caecus, et mendicus
erat.</HI>  Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quoniam mendicus erat. et caecus</HI></P> <P COM="0883">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ille homo, qui dicitur</HI>  JESUS. Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aænqrwpoû
legovmenoû 1Ihsouðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">homo, qui dicitur</HI>  JESUS. Et ita
Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0883">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non est hic homo a Deo, qui sabbatum non
custodit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oÝti toú savbbaton ouj threið,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quia sabbatum
non custodit.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia sabbatum non
observat.</HI>  Verc. et Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0883">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid dicis de illo, qui aperuit oculos tuos?</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti hænoixe,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quia aperuit:</HI>  et ita Brix.; Verc. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quod aperuit.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut si quis eum confiteretur esse Christum.</HI>  In
Graeco non est verbum  <HI REND="ITALIC">esse,</HI>  nec legitur in Veron.,
Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0883">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dixi vobis jam, et audistis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú oujk
hjkouvsate,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et non audistis.</HI>  Et ita Gat., Brix. et Verc.</P> <P COM="0883">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Respondit ille homo.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpekrivqh oJ aænqrwpoû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">respondit homo.</HI>  Et ita Verc. absque pronomine
 <COL N="0883B"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkeiðnoû.</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ille.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et procidens adoravit eum.</HI>  In Graeco, non est
verbum  <HI REND="ITALIC">procidens</HI> : nec in Verc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0883">CAP. X.</CAPTION> <P COM="0883">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Omnes quotquot venerunt.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnteû oåsoi prov ejmouð hølqon,</FOREIGN>  cum Gat., . . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">venerunt
ante me.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et abundantius habeant.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú perissoún
eæcwsin.</FOREIGN>  Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et amplius habeant.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pro ovibus suis.</HI>  In Graeco non est illud pronomen,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">suis:</HI>  nec in Verc. et Brix. Sic versu 15,
ubi legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro ovibus meis,</HI>  in Graeco non est illud,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">meis:</HI>  neque in Verc.</P> <P COM="0883">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non pertinet ad eum de ovibus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj
mevlei aujtwðé periú twðn probavtwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non est illi cura de ovibus.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0883">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Loquor vobis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiøpon uJmiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dixi vobis.</HI> 
Et ita Verc. Tamen in Cantabrig. ms. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>lalwð
uJmiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">loquor vobis.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non estis ex ovibus meis.</HI>  Graece additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaqwðû
eiøpon uJmiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sicut dixi vobis.</HI>  Et ita in Verc., Veron.
 <COL N="0883C"></COL> et Brix. nec non Syrus, atque omnes Graeci codices.</P> <P COM="0883">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sustulerunt ergo lapides Judaei.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejbavstasan
ouøn pavlin livqouû oiJ 1Ioudaiðoi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sustulerunt ergo iterum
lapides Judaei.</HI>  Et ita Brix. Non est tamen illud
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavlin,</FOREIGN>  in Cantabrig. ms.</P> <CAPTION COM="0883">CAP. XI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0883">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Silentio.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>lavqra,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">clam, occulte.</HI> 
Et ita Brix. At in Cantabrigiensi,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>siwphðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">silentio.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Surgit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgeivretai.</FOREIGN>  In Cantabrigiensi,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgevrqh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">surrexit</HI>  Et ita in Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0883">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui aperuit oculos caeci nati.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touúû
ojfqalmouúû touð tuflouð,</FOREIGN>  absque verbo  <HI REND="ITALIC">nati.</HI>  Et ita in
Verc., Veron, et Brix.</P> <P COM="0883">41.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tulerunt ergo lapidem.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouø
høn</FOREIGN>  (in Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi fuerat</HI> )  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>teqnhkwúû keivmenoû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0883">41.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Elevatis sursum.</HI>  Aliqui mss. habent pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">sursum,</HI> 
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû toún oujranoún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in coelum,</HI>  ut Brix. Veron. vero,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ad coelum.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">45.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui venerant ad Mariam et Martham.</HI>  Graeci
non habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Martham;</HI>  deest quoque in Verc.,
 <COL N="0883D"></COL> Veron., Brix., Gat. et Mm.</P> <CAPTION COM="0883">CAP. XII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0883">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ubi Lazarus fuerat mortuus, quem
suscitavit</HI>  JESUS. Graece legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåpou høn Lavzaroû oJ
teqnhkwúû, oÝn eægeiren ejk nekrwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi erat Lazarus, qui
mortuus fuerat, quem suscitavit ex mortuis.</HI>  Brix. habet:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi erat Lazarus, qui fuerat mortuus, quem suscitavit
Jesus ex mortuis.</HI>  Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi erat Lazarus, qui fuit
mortuus, quem suscitavit.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Judas Iscariotes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iouvdaû Sivmwnoû 1Iskariwvthû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Judas Simonis Iscariotes.</HI>  Et ita Corb. sed pro
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Iscariotes</HI>  legit  <HI REND="ITALIC">Iscariotis.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Simonis Schariotes.</HI> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Simon . . . . Scarioth.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Simon Scariotes.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non quia de egenis pertinebat ad eum.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujc oåti periú twðn ptwcwðn eæmelen aujtwðé.</FOREIGN>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">non quia
de pauperibus cura ei erat.</HI>  Verc. et Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non quod
de pauperibus cura illi esset.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et loculos habens.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>glwssovkomon.</FOREIGN> 
Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">loculum.</HI></P> <P COM="0883">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sinite illam, ut in diem sepulturae meae servet illud.</HI> 
 <COL N="0884A"></COL> Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæfeû aujthún, eijû thún hJmevran touð ejntafiasmouð
mou tethvrhken aujtoú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sine illam, in diem sepulturae
meae servavit illud.</HI>  Et ita Brix.; at pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">in diem,</HI> 
legit  <HI REND="ITALIC">in die.</HI>  Veron. quoque et mss. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sine,</HI>  etc.
Graecam editionem Grotius, aliique Latinae anteponunt.
Tamen Latinam absolvunt codices Cantabrigiensis,
Vaticanus, et alii, in quibus legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna
eijû thún hJmevran touð ejntafiasmouð mou thrhvshé aujtov.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0884">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quando Lazarum vocavit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti.</FOREIGN>  Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quia;</HI>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quoniam,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0884">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quia nihil proficimus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wjfeleiðte,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">proficitis.</HI> 
Et ita Verc.; at Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">prodestis.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quidam Gentiles.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>4Ellhneû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Graeci.</HI>  Et
ita Verc., Corb. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0884">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Honorificabit eum Pater meus.</HI>  In Graeco non
est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">meus,</HI>  nec legitur in Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0884">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Clarifica nomen tuum.</HI>  In Cantabrig. ms. legitur:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Dovxason (toún UiJovn sou) ejn thðé dovxhé hßé eiøcon parav soi proú
touðton kovsmon genevsqai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">clarifica Filium tuum</HI>  (Et ita
in mss.)  <HI REND="ITALIC">in gloria, quam habui apud te priusquam
 <COL N="0884B"></COL> mundus fieret.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nunc judicium est mundi.</HI>  Graece additur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvtou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hujus:</HI>  et ita in Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0884">47.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et non custodierit.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú mhú pisteuvshé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et
non crediderit.</HI>  Et ita Brix. Tamen in Alexandrino et
Cantabrig. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú mhú fulavxhé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et non custodierit.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0884">CAP. XIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0884">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et dixit ei: Quis est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>puqevsqai
tivû aÞn eiæh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">interrogare, quis esset.</HI>  Verc. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">interroga, qui est.</HI>  Brix., Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">interroga, quis est.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Introivit in eum Satanas.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tovte eijshðlqen,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">tunc introivit.</HI>  In Brix. quoque et Gat. legitur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">tunc,</HI>  etc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0884">CAP. XIV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0884">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Creditis in Deum, et in me credite.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pisteuvete eijû toún Qeoún, kaiú eijû ejmeú pisteuvete</FOREIGN> :
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Credite in Deum, et in me credite.</HI>  Et ita Veron., Verc.,
Gat. et Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">credite in Deum,</HI>  etc. At Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et in me
creditis.</HI>  Sic Graece positum verbum istud,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pisteuvete,</FOREIGN> 
anceps est: potest enim esse indicativi modi et imperativi.</P> <P COM="0884"><COL N="0884C"></COL> 9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui videt me, videt et Patrem.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ eJwrakwúû
ejmeú, ejwvrake toún Patevra,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui vidit me, vidit Patrem.</HI>  Et
ita Veron., Verc. et Brix.; sed ante  <HI REND="ITALIC">Patrem,</HI>  addunt
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et.</HI>  In Brix. legitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">me,</HI>  post  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non creditis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj pisteuveiû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non credis.</HI> 
Et ita Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0884">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non creditis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pisteuvetev moi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">credite
mihi.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0884">CAP. XV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0884">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tollet eum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aiærei aujtoún,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">tollit eum.</HI>  Et ita Veron., Brix. et Verc. Et mox,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaqaivrei,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">purgat,</HI>  cum Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0884">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jam non dicam vos.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujkevti uJmaðû levgw,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">jam non dico vos.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Veron., Brix. et Gat.;
at mss. . . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">dico vobis.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0884">CAP. XVI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0884">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Obsequium se praestare Deo.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>latreivan prosfevrein twðé Qewðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sacrificium offerre Deo.</HI> 
Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0884">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non crediderunt in me.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ouj pisteuvousin,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">non credunt,</HI>  etc. Et ita Corb. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0884"><COL N="0884D"></COL> 13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Docebit vos omnem veritatem.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJdhghvsei
uJmaðû eijû paðsan thún ajlhvqeian,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">deducet vos in omnem
veritatem.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et Corb.; at Veron. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deducet vos in veritate omni.</HI>  Brix. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">diriget vos
in omnem veritatem.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed tristitia vestra vertetur in gaudium.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJ luvph uJmwðn eijû caraún genhvsetai.</FOREIGN>  Brix. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in gaudium
erit.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nemo tollet a vobis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujdeiúû aiærei aæf1
uJmwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nemo tollit a vobis.</HI>  Et ita Veron. Etiam in
Brix. legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">aufert.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0884">CAP. XVIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0884">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nazarenum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Nazwraiðon.</FOREIGN> 
Veron. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nazoreum.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0884">CAP. XIX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0884">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et veniebant ad eum.</HI>  Haec verba
non habent Graeci codices, nec Brix.</P> <P COM="0884">34.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Latus ejus aperuit.</HI>  In Graeco est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eænuxe,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vulneravit.</HI> 
Et ita in Veron.; at Verc. et Corb. habent,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">percussit.</HI></P> <P COM="0884">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Videbunt in quem transfixerunt.</HI>  In Graeco
 <COL N="0885A"></COL> LXX, Zach. XII, 10, legitur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejpiblevyontai provû
me ajnq1 wßn katwrchvsanto,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et aspicient ad me, quoniam</HI> 
(vel,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro eo quod) insultaverunt.</HI>  Sed apud Aquilam,
Symmachum, et Theodotionem,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû oÝn ejxekevnthsan.</FOREIGN> 
In Verc., Veron. et Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in quem compunxerunt.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0885">CAP. XX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0885">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et vidit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>blevpei,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">videt.</HI>  Et
ita Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0885">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et latus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú thún pleuraún aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et
latus suum.</HI>  Et ita Gat. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0885">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fixuram clavorum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toún tuvpon twðn hålwn,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">figuram clavorum.</HI>  Et ita Veron. Similiter pro eo quod
est in Latino,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et mittam digitum meum in locum clavorum,</HI> 
Graece legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû toún tuvpon twðn hålwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in figuram
clavorum.</HI>  Ab auctore nostrae Latinae editionis
Vulgatae lectum est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tovpon,</FOREIGN>  non  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tuvpon.</FOREIGN></P> <CAPTION COM="0885">CAP. XXI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0885">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et nemo audebat discumbentium.</HI> 
Graece: . . .  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejtovlma twðn maqhtwðn.</FOREIGN>  Verc. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">audebat
ex discipulis.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">discentium audebat.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sic eum volo manere.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæan aujtoún qevlw
mevnein,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">si eum volo manere.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0885"><HEAD COM="0885">S. LUCAS.</HEAD> <COL N="0885B"></COL> <CAPTION COM="0885">CAP. I.</CAPTION> <P COM="0885">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ministri fuerunt sermonis.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð lovgou.</FOREIGN>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">verbi.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Visum est et mihi.</HI>  In quodam ms. Cantuariensi
Graeco hoc loco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú Pneuvmati aJgivwé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et Spiritui
sancto,</HI>  ut etiam in Veron.</P> <P COM="0885">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et timor irruit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnevpesen.</FOREIGN>  Veron. et
Brix. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cecidit.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae cum audisset.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJ deú ijdouðsa.</FOREIGN>  Gat.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsa autem cum vidisset.</HI>  Veron. quoque, Verc.,
Brix. et Corb. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsa autem ut vidit.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qualis esset ista salutatio.</HI>  Addit hoc loco quidem
ms. codex Cantuariensis,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti ouåtwû eujlovghsen
aujthvn.</FOREIGN>  Veron., Brix. et Corb. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod sic benedixisset
eum.</HI>  Quam lectionem etiam Verc. habuisse
videtur, licet quaedam litterae nunc sint oblitteratae,
nec amplius legi possint.</P> <P COM="0885">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quod nascetur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tov gennwvmenon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quod
 <COL N="0885C"></COL> nascitur.</HI>  Et ita Gat. Sed videtur, quod futuri temporis
verbo usus sit angelus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod nascetur.</HI>  Neque
enim de conceptione Christi hoc loco agitur, sed de
nativitate ipsa: alioquin diceret Angelus,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod in
te,</HI>  non  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod ex te;</HI>  ut Matth. I, 20:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quod enim in
ea natum est.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">50.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et misericordia ejus a progenie in progenies,
timentibus eum;</HI>  ut in psalmo CII, 17:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Misericordia
autem Domini ab aeterno, et usque in aeternum super
timentes eum.</HI>  In Graeco est:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú toú eæleoû aujtouð eijû geneaúû
genewðn.</FOREIGN>  Verc. et Veron. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et misericordia
ejus in saecula saeculorum.</HI>  Alii mss. legunt,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû geneaún
kaiú geneaún,</FOREIGN>  cum Corb. et Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in progeniem et
progeniem.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">63.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Joannes est nomen ejus.</HI>  Hic addit ms. Cantabrigiensis:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú paracrhðma hjluvqh hJ glwðssa aujtouð.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. quoque,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et confestim soluta est lingua ejus.</HI> 
Item Veron. et Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et continuo resoluta est lingua
ejus.</HI>  Quamobrem versu sequente omittunt haec verba,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">illico et lingua ejus.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0885">CAP. II.</CAPTION> <COL N="0885D"></COL> <P COM="0885">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">A Praeside.</HI>  In Graeco legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJgemoneuvontoû
thðû Surivaû Kurhnivou.</FOREIGN>  In Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praeside Syriae
Cyrino.</HI>  Qui nomine  <HI REND="ITALIC">universi Orbis</HI>  Romanum omne
imperium intelligi versu primo voluerunt, ii arbitrati,
dici non potuisse factam a Praeside Syriae descriptionem
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hanc</HI>  universi Orbis, ut appellatur versu
isto secundo, praepositionem  <HI REND="ITALIC">a</HI>  expunxere in suis
exemplaribus: ut facta tantum intelligeretur, quo
tempore esset ille Syriae praeses, non tamen ab ipso.</P> <P COM="0885">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Judaeam.</HI>  Ms. Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû ghðn 1Iouvda,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in
terram Juda.</HI>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in terram Judaeam.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Stetit juxta illos.</HI>  In Graeco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpevsth aujtoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">astitit
illis.</HI>  Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0885">Eodem.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et claritas Dei.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dovxa Kurivou.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
quoque, et Brix. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Domini.</HI></P> <P COM="0885">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">De puero hoc.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>periú touð paidivou touvtou.</FOREIGN> 
Sed illud  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touvtou</FOREIGN>  non habent mss. Cantabrigiensis,
Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0885"><COL N="0886A"></COL> 18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et omnes qui audierunt, mirati sunt, et de his,
quae dicta erant a pastoribus ad ipsos.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejqauvmasan
periú twðn lalhqevntwn,</FOREIGN>  etc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">mirati sunt de his,
quae dicta erant,</HI>  etc., expuncta particula conjunctiva
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et,</HI>  quae deest etiam in Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0886">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et Spiritus sanctus erat in eo.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejp1 aujton,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">super eum</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0886">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Parentes ejus.</HI>  Illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">ejus,</HI>  Graeci libri nulli habent;
sed  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>goneiðû</FOREIGN>  tantum, ante  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toú paidivon,</FOREIGN>  ut Verc.</P> <P COM="0886">33.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et erat pater ejus, et mater.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú høn
1Iwshúf kaiú hJ mhvthr aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et erat Joseph, et mater ejus.</HI> 
Et ita in Verc., Corb., Veron. et Brix. In Cantabrigiensi
vero ms. legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú høn pathúr kaiú hJ mhvthr,</FOREIGN> 
absque  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ejus.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">34.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et in signum, cui contradicetur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajntilegovmenon</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod contradicitur.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Redemptionem Israel.</HI>  Graeci codices et Gothica
versio,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>luvtrwsin ejn 1Ierousalhúm.</FOREIGN>  Veron. et Brix. legunt,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">redemptionem Hierusalem.</HI>  Et ita Corb.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Jerusalem.</HI></P> <P COM="0886"><COL N="0886B"></COL> 40.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et confortabatur.</HI>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">confortabatur spiritu;</HI> 
ut habet idem S. Lucas etiam cap. I, 80, de Joanne:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Puer autem crescebat, et confortabatur spiritu.
Confortandi</HI>  verbum interdum in sacris Litteris de
viribus corporis accipitur; ut Act. IX, 19:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et cum
accepisset cibum,</HI>  CONFORTATUS EST. Quare nonnulli
Graeci codices legunt hoc loco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejkrataiouðto pneuvmati,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">confortabatur spiritu.</HI>  Quamquam in Cantabrigiensi
ms. vox illa non apparet.</P> <P COM="0886">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Secundum consuetudinem diei festi.</HI>  Addit ms.
Cantabrigiensis:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>twðn 1Azuvmwn.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Azymorum.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">43.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Parentes ejus.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>1Iwshúf kaiú hJ mhvthr
aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Joseph, et mater ejus,</HI>  ut versu 33. Et ita in
Corb., Veron. et Brix. Cantabrigiensis habet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ goneiðû
aujtouð.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0886">45.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Requirentes.</HI>  Graece,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>zhtouðnteû.</FOREIGN>  Verc. et Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quaerentes.</HI>  Cantabrigiensis,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnazhtouðnteû.</FOREIGN></P> <CAPTION COM="0886">CAP. III.</CAPTION> <P COM="0886">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut baptizarentur ab ipso.</HI>  In Cantabrigiensi
ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejnwvpion aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">coram ipso.</HI>  Et ita in Veron.</P> <P COM="0886"><COL N="0886C"></COL> 8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ne caeperitis dicere.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú mhú
aærxhsqe levgein ejn eJautoiðû.</FOREIGN>  In Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ne incipiatis dicere
intra vos.</HI>  In Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú mhú dovxhte levgein ejn
eJautoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et ne putetis dicere intra vos.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid ergo faciemus?</HI>  In Cantabrig. ms. additur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna swqwðmen,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut salvemur,</HI>  quod iterum repetitur versu
14. Veron. et Gat. habent  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut vivamus.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Existimante autem populo.</HI>  In Graeco (etiam ms.
Cantabr.):  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Prosdokwðntoû deú touð laouð.</FOREIGN>  In Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sperante
autem populo.</HI>  Putant nonnulli, quod Vulgatus interpres
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dokouðntoû</FOREIGN>  legerit, pro  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prosdokwðntoû</FOREIGN> ; vel, quod
amanuensis Latinus scripserit  <HI REND="ITALIC">existimante,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">exspectante.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Veniet autem.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eærcetai dev.</FOREIGN> 
In Verc., Brix. et Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">venit autem.</HI>  In Cantabrig.,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ deú ejrcovmenoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui autem venit.</HI>  Et sic ubicumque legitur
in Latina edit.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui venturus est,</HI>  in Graeco est,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ ejrcovmenoû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0886">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fratris sui.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Filivppou,</FOREIGN> 
qua voce alii mss. Graeci sat multi carent, uti
 <COL N="0886D"></COL> etiam nostri Latini Veron., Verc. et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0886">CAP. IV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0886">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Agebatur a spiritu.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hægeto ejn
twðé pneuvmati,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">agebatur in spiritu.</HI>  Et ita Corb. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0886">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Diebus quadraginta, et tentabatur a diabolo.</HI>  In
Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJmevraû tessavrakonta peirazovmenoû.</FOREIGN>  Verc. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">diebus</HI>  XXXX  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum temptaretur.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">diebus</HI>  XXXX
 <HI REND="ITALIC">temptabatur.</HI>  Gat. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">temptatur.</HI></P> <P COM="0886">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Esuriit.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåsteron ejpeivnase,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">postea
esuriit.</HI>  Et ita Brix. In Cantabrig. tamen non est illud,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåsteron.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0886">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dic lapidi huic, ut panis fiat.</HI>  In Cantabrigiensi,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna oiJ livqoi oußtoi aærtoi gevnwntai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut lapides isti panes
fiant.</HI>  Verc. quoque videtur legisse,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fiant panes.</HI>  Forte
ex Matthaeo.</P> <P COM="0886">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Orbis terrae.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðû oijkoumevnhû.</FOREIGN> 
In Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kovsmou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mundi:</HI>  et ita in Brix. ex
Matthaeo.</P> <P COM="0886">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dicit illi.</HI>  Hic addunt Graeci libri Vulgati:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uåpage</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0887A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ojpivsw mou, Satanað,</FOREIGN>  cum Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vade post me, Satanas.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et magnificabatur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>doxazovmenoû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">honorem accipiens.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sanare contritos corde.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praedicare captivis remissionem, et caecis visum,
dimittere confractos in remissionem.</HI>  Origenes, Eusebius,
Augustinus et Beda, omittunt priorem sententiam;
posteriorem, retenta priore, Theophylactus.
Hieronymus in caput LXI Isaiae, citans hunc
Lucae locum, servat utramque. Mss. Graeci nonnulli,
quos citat Lucas Brugensis, et codex Cantabrig.
omittunt illud,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sanare contritos corde,</HI>  cum Verc.,
Veron. et Corb., tametsi est apud Isaiam.</P> <P COM="0887">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In domum Simonis.</HI>  Addit Cantabrig. ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú
1Andrevou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et Andreae.</HI>  Et ita Corb. et Veron. ex
Marc. I, 29.</P> <P COM="0887">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Magnis febribus.</HI>  In Graeco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunecomevnh</FOREIGN>  (in
Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>katecomevnh) puretwðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">febre magna,</HI>  ut habet
Verc. Corb. quoque legit in singulari numero,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">febri.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0887">CAP. V.</CAPTION> <COL N="0887B"></COL> <P COM="0887">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum turbae irruerent in eum.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé toún oæclon ejpikeiðsqai aujtwðé.</FOREIGN>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dum
turba incumbit ei.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Descenderant.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpobavnteû ajp1 aujtwðn.</FOREIGN> 
Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">descendentes de eis.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praeceptor.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpistavta,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">praeses, praefecte,
qui praees et praecipis, qui positus es ad praecipiendum.</HI> 
Tamen ms. Cantabrig. habet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>didavskale,</FOREIGN>  cum
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">magister.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rumpebatur autem rete.</HI>  Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wåste taú divktua
rJhvssesqai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ita ut retia rumperentur.</HI>  Brix. quoque
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ita ut rumperentur retiae.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ita ut pene mergerentur.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato non
legitur illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">pene;</HI>  nec in Verc., Corb., Veron. aut
Brix. In ms. Cantabrig. est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>parav ti.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0887">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eris capiens.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæshé zwgrwðn.</FOREIGN>  Veron. et
Verc. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">eris vivificans.</HI>  Corb. quoque legit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vivificans.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nisi solus Deus?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij mhú movnoû oJ Qeovû,</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0887C"></COL> Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eij mhú eißû oJ Qeoúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nisi unus Deus.</HI>  Et ita
Verc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0887">CAP. VI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0887">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et restituta est manus ejus.</HI>  In
Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJgihúû wJû hJ aællh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sana sicut altera.</HI> 
In Brix. quoque habetur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sicut altera,</HI>  et in Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sicut alia.</HI>  Ex Matth. XII, 13. In Alexandrino ms.
aliisque additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJgihúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sana,</HI>  tantum.</P> <P COM="0887">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et Tyri.</HI>  Deest conjunctio  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú,</FOREIGN>  in Graeco, atque
in Verc., Corb. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0887">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ipse in oculo tuo trabem non videns.</HI>  Ms. Cantabrig.,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ijdouú hJ dovkoû ejn twðé swðé ojfqalmwðé uJpovkeitai.</FOREIGN> 
Verc., Veron. et Corb. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ecce in oculo tuo</HI> 
(Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">suo) trabes</HI>  (Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">trabis) subjacet.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">45.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Os loquitur.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>laleið toú stovma aujtouð,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">loquitur os ejus.</HI>  Et ita Corb., Veron. et Brix. Verc.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">illius.</HI>  Sed in Cantabrig. non est illud,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð.</FOREIGN></P> <CAPTION COM="0887">CAP. VII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0887">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad</HI>  JESUM. In Cantabrig. ms. deest
illud,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>proúû toún 1Ihsouðn,</FOREIGN>  ut etiam in Verc. Sed in
Graeco Vulgato legitur.</P> <P COM="0887"><COL N="0887D"></COL> 9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sequentibus se turbis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>twðé ajkolouqouðnti
aujtwðé oæclwé.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sequenti se turbae.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Amen dico vobis.</HI>  Non est illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">amen,</HI>  in
Graeco Vulgato, nec in Veron.; at est in Cantabrigiensi.</P> <P COM="0887">Eodem.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Israel.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujdeú ejn twðé 1Israhvl.</FOREIGN>  Brix.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nec in Isdrahel.</HI>  Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujdevpote,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">numquam.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Deinceps.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn thðé eJxhðû.</FOREIGN>  In Alexandrino
ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hjn twðé eJxhðû.</FOREIGN>  Brix. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in sequenti die.</HI></P> <P COM="0887">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ibant cum eo discipuli ejus.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ
maqhtaiú aujtouð iJkanoiú,</FOREIGN>  cum Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">discipuli ejus
multi:</HI>  ut alii, praeter duodecim, comitati tunc
fuisse JESUM existimentur.</P> <P COM="0887">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ecce defunctus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ijdouv,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et ecce.</HI>  Et ita
Brix., Veron. et Verc.</P> <P COM="0887">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Matris suae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thðé mhtriú aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">matri
suae.</HI>  Et ita Brix. Dandi casus significat superstitem
 <COL N="0888A"></COL> matri suae unicum: non quem unicum pepererit mater
sua.</P> <P COM="0888">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Magnificabant Deum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejdovxazon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">glorificabant,</HI> 
ut alibi superius. Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0888">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In universam Judaeam.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn oålhé thðé
1Ioudaivaé.</FOREIGN>  Et ita in Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in tota Judaea.</HI>  Veron. quoque
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in universa Judaea.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et plagis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú mastivgwn,</FOREIGN>  cum Verc.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et verberibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mulier, quae erat in civitate peccatrix.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gunhú ejn thðé povlei, håtiû høn aJmartwloúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mulier in civitate,
quae erat peccatrix.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0888">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis ergo eum plus diligit?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tivû ouøn
aujtwðn.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quis ergo eorum,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0888">44.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Intravi domum tuam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijshðlqovn sou eijû
thún oijkivan,</FOREIGN>  juxta Verc., Veron. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">intravi</HI> 
(Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">introivi) in domum tuam.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0888">CAP. VIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0888">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">A spiritibus malignis.</HI>  In quodam
ms. Graec.:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoú novswn.</FOREIGN>  In Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ab infirmitatibus,</HI>  etc.
In Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">infirmitatibus,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0888"><COL N="0888B"></COL> 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae ministrabant ei.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðé,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ei.</HI>  At in Cantabrig. et altero Rob. Stephani ms.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoiðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">eis:</HI>  ut legunt Brix. et Gat. et habetur similiter
in Syriaca versione: ut ad Apostolos referatur
simul, et ad Christum.</P> <P COM="0888">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum autem turba plurima convenirent.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunivontoû dhú oæclou.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">conveniente autem turba.</HI> 
Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunelqovntoû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0888">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dixit per similitudinem.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Diaú parabolhðû.</FOREIGN> 
In Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eiøpe parabolhún tauvthn proúû aujtouvû.</FOREIGN> 
In Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dixit similitudinem ad illos talem.</HI>  In Verc.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">dixit parabolam,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0888">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vir quidam.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk thðû povlewû.</FOREIGN> 
In Veron. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de civitate.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Is ut vidit</HI>  JESUM. In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ijdwún deú toún 1Ihsouðn,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">videns autem</HI>  JESUM. Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0888">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Obsecro te.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>devomaiv sou.</FOREIGN>  Vercellens.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">oro te.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et contigit, dum iret, a turbis comprimebatur.</HI> 
 <COL N="0888C"></COL> Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn deú twðé uJpavgein aujtoún, oiJ oæcloi sunevpnigon aujtoún.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dum iret turba . . . ut suffocarent eum.</HI> 
Corb. . . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">comprimebatur, ut suffocarent eum.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">47.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et procidit ante pedes ejus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú prospesouðsa
aujtwðé.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et procidit ante eum.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">49.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad principem Synagogae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paraú touð
ajrcisunagwvgou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">a principe Synagogae.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et
Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0888">CAP. IX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0888">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Duodecim Apostolis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touúû
dwvdeka maqhtaúû auJtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">duodecim discipulis suis.</HI>  Et
ita Veron. At Cantabrigiensis ms. et Alexandrinus,
et alii multi habent dumtaxat,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touúû dwvdeka,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">duodecim.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et inde ne exeatis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejkeiðqen ejxevrcesqe,</FOREIGN> 
juxta Verc., Veron. et Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et inde</HI>  (Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">exite)
proficiscimini.</HI>  At Luc. X, 7:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nolite transire de domo
in domum.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui est Bethsaidae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû tovpon eærhmon
povlewû kaloumevnhû Bhqsaiçdaú,</FOREIGN>  juxta Verc. et Brix., qui
 <COL N="0888D"></COL> legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in locum desertum, qui vocabatur</HI>  (in Brix.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">dicitur) Bethsaida.</HI>  Gat. quoque habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bethsaida.</HI> 
Veron. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Betsaida.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In omnem hanc turbam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû pavnta toún
laoún touðton,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in omnem hunc populum.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0888">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et Jacobum, et Joannem.</HI>  In Graeco, nominum
ordine permutato.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú 1Iwavnnhn, kaiú 1Iavkwbon.</FOREIGN>  Et
ita in Veron., Verc., Brix. et Gat. At ms. Cantabrigiensis
Vulgatam editionem sequitur.</P> <P COM="0888">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Excessum ejus.</HI>  Graece est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thún eæxodon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">exitum.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0888">36.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et dum fieret vox.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejn twðé genevsqai
thún fwnhún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et cum facta esset vox.</HI>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
cum facta est vox.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Obsecro te.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>devomaiv sou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">oro te,</HI>  ut
Vercellensis</P> <P COM="0888">39.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et dissipat eum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>spavrassei aujtoún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">discerpit
eum.</HI>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">discarpit illum.</HI></P> <P COM="0888">44.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In cordibus vestris.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû taú wøta uJmwðn.</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0889A"></COL> Verc., Veron., Brix. et Corb. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in auribus
vestris.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">48.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hic major est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oußtoû eæstai mevgaû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hic
erit magnus.</HI>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hic est magnus.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">54.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et consumat illos.</HI>  Addunt Graeci codices:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû
kaiú 1Hlivaû ejpoivhse,</FOREIGN>  cum Verc., Veron. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sicut
Helias</HI>  (Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et Helias) fecit.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">56.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Animas perdere.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>yucaúû ajnqrwvpwn,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">animas hominum.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">57.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quocumque ieris.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kuvrie,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Domine.</HI>  Et ita in Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0889">CAP. X.</CAPTION> <P COM="0889">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Septuaginta duos.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eJbdomhvkonta</FOREIGN>  tantum, hoc est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">septuaginta.</HI>  Et ita
in Veron., Brix. et Syriaca versione. In ms. Cantabrig.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ob',</FOREIGN>  hoc est,  <HI REND="ITALIC">septuaginta duo.</HI>  In alio ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ov maqhtaúû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">septuaginta discipulos.</HI>  Forte ut cum Septuaginta
senibus ex Israel, quorum mentio est Num. XI,
16, 24, 25, conferri isti possent, et cum septuaginta
palmis, quae in Elim juxta aquas fontium duodecim
creverant, Graeci libri quidam manuscripti non
 <COL N="0889B"></COL> LXXII, sed LXII, legerunt in hoc Lucae loco.</P> <P COM="0889">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad vos revertetur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejf1 uJmaðû,</FOREIGN>  etc. Verc.
et Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">super vos,</HI>  etc. At in Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejf1 uJmaðû
ajnastrevyei hJ eijrhvnh uJmwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in vos convertetur pax
vestra.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Etiam pulverem, qui adhaesit nobis.</HI>  Alexandrinus,
et Cantabrig. ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû touúû povdaû hJmwðn.</FOREIGN> 
Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in pedibus nostris.</HI>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in pedes.</HI>  Veron.,
Mm. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in pedibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Septuaginta duo.</HI>  Graece:  <HI REND="ITALIC">septuaginta</HI>  tantum,
ut versu I. Et ita Veron., Brix. et Vind.</P> <P COM="0889">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et nihil vobis nocebit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJmaðû ouj mhú ajdikhvsei.</FOREIGN> 
Verc., Veron. et Vind., . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">vos nocebit.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In coelis.</HI>  Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé oujranwðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in coelo.</HI>  Et
ita Verc., Veron., Brix. et Vindeb.</P> <P COM="0889">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In quoddam castellum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû kwvmhn tinav.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in vicum quemdam.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0889">CAP. XI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0889">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adveniat regnum tuum.</HI>  In Graeco
hic additur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fiat voluntas tua, sicut in coelo, et in
 <COL N="0889C"></COL> terra.</HI>  Et ita in Vindeb., Brix. et versione Syriaca.
In Veron. quoque legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fiat voluntas tua in coelo,
et in terra.</HI>  In Verc. tantum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fiat voluntas tua.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In tentationem.</HI>  Addunt Graeci codices, ut sit integra
hic oratio, qualis est apud Matthaeum,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajllaú
rJuðsai hJmaðû ajpoú touð ponhrouð.</FOREIGN>  Corb. et Veron. quoque
habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed libera nos a malo.</HI>  Vind. et Brix.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sed erue</HI>  (Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">eripe) nos a malo.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In cubili.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû thún koivthn.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Vind.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">in cubilem.</HI>  Cantabrig. tamen,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn thðé koivthé.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0889">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis autem ex vobis patrem petit panem,</HI>  etc.
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tivna deú uJmwðn toún patevra aijthvsei oJ uiJovû.</FOREIGN>  Brix.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quem autem ex vobis patrem, si petierit filius.</HI> 
Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">a quo autem ex vobis petet filius.</HI>  Vind. et
Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">a quo autem patre ex vobis petet filius.</HI>  Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex
vobis patrem petiit filius.</HI>  Mss.  <HI REND="ITALIC">exvobis filius patri petiit.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Beelzebub.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn Beelzebouúl,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in
Beelzebul:</HI>  Et ita Vindeb. et Brix.; at Veron. et Gat.
habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Belzebul.</HI>  Corb. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Belsebul.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pervenit in vos regnum Dei.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæfqasen</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0889D"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejf1 uJmaðû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">praevenit ad vos.</HI>  Veron. et Brix. habent,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">praevenit in vos,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0889">41.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quod superest.</HI>  Graece legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú ejnovnta.</FOREIGN>  Quod
verbum alii vertunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae suppetunt, quae penes vos
sunt:</HI>  alii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae intus exsistunt:</HI>  alii,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae sunt;</HI>  ut
habet cod. Veronensis.</P> <P COM="0889">44.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vae vobis.</HI>  In Graeco additur:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>grammateiðû, kaiú
Farisaiðoi uJpokritaiú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Scribae et Pharisaei hypocritae.</HI> 
Et ita in Veron., Brix. et Vind. qui tamen omittit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">hypocritae.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">49.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mittam ad illos.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû aujtouúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in illos.</HI> 
Et ita Vind. et Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0889">CAP. XII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0889">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Multis autem turbis circumstantibus.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpisunacqeiswðn.</FOREIGN>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">congregatis.</HI></P> <P COM="0889">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Attendite.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prwðton prosevcete eJautoiðû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">primum attendite vobis a fermento.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">primo
attendite vobis a fermento.</HI>  Veron., . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">vobis . . .</HI>  Verc.
et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">primum . . .</HI></P> <P COM="0889"><COL N="0890A"></COL> 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nihil autem.</HI>  In Cantabrig.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujdeún gaúr,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nihil
enim.</HI>  Et ita in Verc.</P> <P COM="0890">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In lumine dicentur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn fwtiú ajkousqhvsetai,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">in lumine audientur.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0890">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In cubiculis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn toiðû tameivoiû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in cellariis.</HI> 
Et ita Vind. ut versu 24,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tameiðon</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cellarium est.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid oporteat vos dicere.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aÝ deið eijpeiðn.</FOREIGN> 
Verc., Veron., Brix. et Vind. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae oportet
dicere.</HI>  Mm.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et majora faciam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oijkodomhvsw,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aedificabo.</HI> 
Et ita Verc. et Brix. Sed in Cantabrig. legitur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poihvsw,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">faciam.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cujus erunt?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tivni eæstai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cui erunt?</HI> 
Et ita Vind. At in Cantabrig. ms.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tivnoû eæstai.</FOREIGN>  Genitivus,
potestatem ac dominium; dativus, usum declarat.</P> <P COM="0890">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quaerite primum.</HI>  Non est illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">primum,</HI>  in
Graeco; nec legitur in Veron., Verc., Brix., Corb.,
Gat. aut Mm.</P> <P COM="0890">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et justitiam ejus.</HI>  Haec quoque desunt in Graeco,
 <COL N="0890B"></COL> et in Verc., Veron., Brix. ac Vind.</P> <P COM="0890">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In manibus vestris.</HI>  Haec verba non sunt in ullo
Graeco codice, sive edito, sive manuscripto, nec in
Verc., Veron., Brix. aut Gat.</P> <P COM="0890">39.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qua hora fur veniret.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eærcetai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">venit.</HI> 
Et ita Veron., Brix. et Vind.</P> <P COM="0890">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quem constituit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oån katasthvshé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quem
constituet.</HI>  Et ita Vind. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0890">49.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et quid volo, nisi ut accendatur?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú tiv
qevlw, eij hædh ajnhvfqh.</FOREIGN>  Veron., Corb. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
quid volo, si accendatur.</HI>  In Corb. tamen et Vind.
deest, etc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0890">CAP. XIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0890">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In Silae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé Silwaúm.</FOREIGN> 
Brix. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siloam.</HI>  Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Syloam.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Terram occupat.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>thún ghðn katargeið.</FOREIGN> 
Veron. et Corb. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">terram evacuat.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et hoc anno.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú touðto toú
eætoû.</FOREIGN> 
In Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et hunc annum.</HI>  In Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæti touðton
toún ejniautoún.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0890"><COL N="0890C"></COL> 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sabbatis.</HI>  In Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>twðé sabbavtwé.</FOREIGN>  Et ita
in Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sabbato.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In synagoga eorum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn miaðé twðn
sunagwgwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in una synagogarum.</HI>  Et ita in Veron.;
sed Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in quadam synagoga.</HI>  Cantabrig. codex
ms. secutus editionem Vulgatam, legit,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn thðé
sunagwghðé aujtwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in synagoga eorum.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vocavit eam ad se.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>prosefwvnhse,</FOREIGN>  tantum.
Brix., Gat., Mm. et Vind. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocavit ad
se.</HI>  At hoc totum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vocavit eam ad se,</HI>  Cantabrigiensis
ms. omittit.</P> <P COM="0890">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hypocritae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpokritaú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hypocrita.</HI>  Et
ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0890">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Filiam Abrahae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>qugatevra 1Abraaúm ouøsan.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum sit filia Abrahae.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum autem intraverit paterfamilias.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajf1 ouß aÞn ejgevrqh.</FOREIGN>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex quo surrexerit.</HI>  Tamen
Cantabrigiensis ms. secutus editionem Vulgatam,
habet,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijsevlqh,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">intraverit.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0890">CAP. XIV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0890">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Homo quidam hydropicus erat ante
 <COL N="0890D"></COL> illum.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>høn uJdrwpikoúû eæmprosqen aujtouð,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">erat hydropicus ante illum.</HI>  In Cantabrig. ms. deest
vox illa,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quidam.</HI>  Et ita in Veron. et Corb.</P> <P COM="0890">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ipse vero apprehensum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejpilabovmenoû.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipse itaque adprehendens.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum invitatus fueris.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpoú
tivnoû.</FOREIGN>  Et ita in Veron. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ab aliquo.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad perficiendum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú proúû ajpartismoún.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae opus sunt ad consummandum.</HI> 
Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae opus sunt ad perficiendum.</HI></P> <P COM="0890">33.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Omnibus quae possidet.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðsi toiðû
eJautouð uJpavrcousi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">omnibus suis facultatibus.</HI>  Et ita
Verc.</P> <P COM="0890">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed foras mittetur.</HI>  Graece, absque particula
adversativa  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed,</HI>   <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>bavllousin aujtovn.</FOREIGN>  Veron. quoque habet
tantum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">mittent eum.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0890">CAP. XV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0890">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Publicani.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnteû oiJ telwðnai,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">omnes publicani.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Brix. et Vind.</P> <P COM="0890"><COL N="0891A"></COL> 14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et postquam omnia consummasset.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dapanhvsantoû deú aujtouð pavnta.</FOREIGN>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cumque
consumpsisset omnia.</HI>  Veron., Brix. et Vind., . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">consumpsit . . .</HI></P> <P COM="0891">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hic fame pereo.</HI>  Abest a Graeco adverbium
istud,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hic,</HI>  quod locum a domo paterna longe dissitum
indicat. Sic etiam ibi scriptum est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>povsoi mivsqioi
patrovû mou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quanti mercenarii patris mei:</HI>  et ita
in Verc., Veron., Brix., Corb., Gat. et Mm. In Vind.
quoque, . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">mercenarii patris . . . ,</HI>  pro eo quod est in
editione Vulgata,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in domo patris mei.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et manducemus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú fagovntes.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et manducantes.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et chorum.</HI>  Graece  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú corwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et choros.</HI>  Et ita
Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0891">CAP. XVI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0891">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Diffamatus est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>dieblhvqh.</FOREIGN> 
Vind. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">delatus erat.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Villicare.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oijkonomeiðn.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">administrare.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Accipe cautionem tuam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gravmma,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">litteras.</HI> 
 <COL N="0891B"></COL> Et ita Veron. et Corb.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cautio</HI>  dicitur, quia
per eas litteras cavetur creditori, ne debitor ei negare
debitum possit.</P> <P COM="0891">9.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mammona.</HI>  Hoc verbo Syriaco significari
divitias, hujus orationis series et  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajkolouqiva</FOREIGN>  admonet.
In Graeco Vulgato scribitur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mamonað×</FOREIGN>  et
ita in Verc., Veron. et Brix. In Cantabrigiensi tamen
ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mammonað.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0891">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui erant avari.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>filavrguroi.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">amatores pecuniae.</HI>  Omnis amor pecuniae a Deo reprehenditur,
qui sit cum avaritia conjunctus.</P> <P COM="0891">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et nemo illi dabat.</HI>  In omnibus libris Graecis
haec desunt; ut etiam in Verc., Veron., et Brix.</P> <P COM="0891">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et sepultus est in inferno.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejtavfh.</FOREIGN> 
Veron. et Brix. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sepultus est.</HI>  Praeclara antithesis
in Latino Vulg. textu fulget: ubi mendici
sors ultima ultimae pariter divitis sorti egregie opponitur:
dum ille, portatus ab Angelis in sinum Abrahae
dicitur; iste, non sepultus tantum, ut in Graeco,
 <COL N="0891C"></COL> et in duobus ex nostris codd. legitur; sed,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sepultus
in inferno.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In aquam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uådatoû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aqua.</HI>  Et ita
Brix.</P> <P COM="0891">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Recepisti bona.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpevlabeû suú taú ajgaqav,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">recepisti tu bona.</HI>  Et ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0891">28.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In hunc locum tormentorum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>basavnou.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cruciatus.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0891">CAP. XVII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0891">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dum irent.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé uJpavgein
aujtouúû.</FOREIGN>  In Veron., Corb., et Vind., legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dum
vadunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gratias agens.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ei.</HI>  Et
ita in Veron.</P> <P COM="0891">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ait ad discipulos suos.</HI>  Deest pronomen
 <HI REND="ITALIC">suos,</HI>  in omnibus libris Graecis, atque in Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0891">CAP. XVIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0891">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Per multum tempus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiú
crovnon.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">per tempus.</HI></P> <P COM="0891">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sugillet me.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpopiavzhé me,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">livore oculos
sugillet.</HI>  Quidam mss. Graeci  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpopievzhé me.</FOREIGN>  Veron.
et Corb. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">constringat me.</HI></P> <P COM="0891"><COL N="0891D"></COL> 7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et patientiam habebit in illis?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>makroquvmwðn
ejp aujtoiðû.</FOREIGN>  Veron., Verc. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">patientiam
habens</HI>  (in Alexandrino ms.,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>makroqumeið</FOREIGN>  Sic
in Graeco Ecclesiastici, cap. XXXV, vers. 18 (qui locus
respondet Editioni Latinae, cap. XXXV, vers. 22)
legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujdeú mhú makroqumhvsei ejn aujtoiðû.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0891">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Putas.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aøra.</FOREIGN>  Veron. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">numquid?</HI></P> <P COM="0891">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Justificatus . . . ab illo. Ab illo utique</HI>  Pharisaeo,
ad quem pronomen  <HI REND="ITALIC">ab illo,</HI>  refertur; et idem valet,
ac  <HI REND="ITALIC">prae illo.</HI>  In Graeco legitur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hæ ejkeiðnos,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quam ille.</HI>  Et
ita in Veron., Brix., Gat., Corb. et Vind. In Cantabrig.
Vero  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>maðllon par1 ejkeiðnon toún Farisaiðon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">magis
supra illum Pharisaeum:</HI>  in aliis  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>par1 ejkeiðnon,</FOREIGN>  dumtaxat.
Verc. habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">prae illum,</HI>  imitatus Graecam syntaxin.</P> <P COM="0891">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et matrem.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sou</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tuam.</HI>  Et
ita in Verc. et Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0891">CAP. XIX.</CAPTION> <P COM="0891">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Divertisset.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijshðlqe kataluðsai</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0892A"></COL> Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">introisset manere.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">intravit
manore.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Servos.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touúû douvlouû touvtouû.</FOREIGN>  In Brix.
legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">servos illos.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut sciret quantum quisque negotiatus esset.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna gnwðé tivû tiv diepragmateuvsato,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut sciret
quis quid negotiatus esset.</HI>  Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut sciret quis
quid negotiatus fuisset.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut ego veniens.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejgwú ejlqwún,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et ego
veniens.</HI>  Et ita Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0892">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et abundabit.</HI>  Istud in Graeco deest, ut etiam
in Verc., Brix., Corb. et Vind.</P> <P COM="0892">28  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praecedebat.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejporeuveto,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ibat.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0892">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Omnes turbae discipulorum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paðû oæcloû,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">omnis multitudo.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0892">39.  <HI REND="ITALIC">De turbis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoú touð oæclou,</FOREIGN>  ut versu 37.
Verc. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de turba.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">43.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Coangustabunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunevxousi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">continebunt.</HI> 
Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0892">47.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Plebis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>laouð</FOREIGN>  Verc., Brix. et Gat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">populi.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0892">CAP. XX.</CAPTION> <COL N="0892B"></COL> <P COM="0892">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Convenerunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpevsthsan.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet:  <HI REND="ITALIC">adstiterunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Respondete mihi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eiæpatev moi,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et dicite
mihi.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0892">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eum in seromone.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð lovgou.</FOREIGN>  Corb. et
Vind.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sermones ejus.</HI>  Verc. . . .  <HI REND="ITALIC">illius.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui negant.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ ajntilevgonteû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui contradicunt
resurrectionem non esse.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0892">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Secus rubum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpiú thðû bavtou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in rubo.</HI> 
Et ita Corb. et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0892">CAP. XXI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0892">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ex abundanti sibi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk touð
perisseuvontoû aujtoiðû.</FOREIGN>  Verc. habet.  <HI REND="ITALIC">de quo super illis
fuit.</HI>  Brix.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ex eo quod abundavit illis.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum fieri incipient.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåtan mevllhé tauðta
givnesqai.</FOREIGN>  Corb. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum futura erunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non praemeditari quemadmodum respondeatis.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhú promeletaðén ajpologhqhðnai.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non prius
meditare, quomodo rationem reddatis.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">A parentibus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú uJpoú gonevwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et a parentibus.</HI> 
 <COL N="0892C"></COL> Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0892">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pressura magna.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnavgkh megavlh.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">necessitas magna.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pressura gentium.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sunochú ejqnwðn.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">compressio gentium.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">occursus gentium.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Arescentibus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajpoyucovntwn.</FOREIGN>  In Verc. legitur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">a refrigescentibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Virtutes coelorum movebuntur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aiJ 
gaúr dunavmeiû twðn oujranwðn saleuqhvsontai.</FOREIGN>  In Cantabrig.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aiJ gaúr dunavmeiû aiJ ejn twðé oujranwðé.</FOREIGN>  In Verc. et Corb.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Virtutes enim</HI>  (in Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nam Virtutes) quae sunt in
coelo.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum potestate magna et majestate.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>metaú dunavmewû kaiú dovxhû pollhðû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum potestate
magna, et gloria.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Producunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>probavlwsin.</FOREIGN>  Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">producant.</HI> 
Additur in Graeco deinde, quod in nostris
Latinis non est;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>blevponteû ejf1 eJautoiðû ginwvskete,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ea
cernentes per vos ipsos agnoscitis.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0892">CAP. XXII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0892">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Timebant vero.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejfobouðnto</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0892D"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>gaúr,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">timebant enim.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et Brix. Cantabrig.
habet cum vulgata editione,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejfobouðnto deú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">timebant
vero.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui cognominabatur.</HI>  In Graeco legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toún ejpikalouvmenon</FOREIGN> ;
ut in Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui cognominatur.</HI>  In Cantabrig.
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toún kalouvmenon.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0892">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">De duodecim.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejk touð ajriqmouð twðn dwvdeka.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de numero</HI>  XII.</P> <P COM="0892">Ibidem, 6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut traderet illum sine turbis.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæter oæclou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sine turba.</HI>  Et ita Verc., Corb., Vindeb.
et Veron.</P> <P COM="0892">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Occidi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>quvesqai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">immolari.</HI>  Et ita Corb.,
Vindeb. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0892">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fiat sicut minor.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>wJû oJ newvteroû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sicut
junior.</HI>  Et ita Gat., Mm. et Brix. Veron. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">adolescentior.</HI></P> <P COM="0892">51.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sinite usque huc.</HI>  Verc., Corb. et Vind. habent,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">usque hoc,</HI>  pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">usque huc,</HI>  cum. Graeco,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mevcri deuðro.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0892"><COL N="0893A"></COL> 52.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et magistratus templi.</HI>  Graeci codices hoc loco
legunt,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>strathgouús.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Antistites.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0893">CAP. XXIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0893">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Constanter.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eujtovnwû.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vehementer.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum exercitu suo.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>suún toiðû strateuvmasin
aujtouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cum exercitibus suis.</HI>  Et ita Veron. et
Corb. Brix. vero habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum militibus suis.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Emendatum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paideuvsaû.</FOREIGN>  Vercell. legit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">castigatum.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Missus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>beblhmevnoû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">conjectus.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Corripiam ergo illum, et dimittam.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>paideuvsaû ouøn aujtoún ajpoluvsw.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">castigatum ergo
illum dimittam.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">emendans ergo illum dimittam.</HI> 
Vide quae diximus ad vers. 16.</P> <P COM="0893">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Instabant.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejpevkeinto,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">imminebant.</HI>  Et
ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0893">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Venient dies.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eærcontai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">veniunt.</HI>  Et ita
Mm. In Cantabrig. est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejleuvsontai.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0893">33.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et latrones.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú touúû kakouvrgouû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et
maleficos.</HI>  Et sic versu 39. Graece est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kakouvrgoiû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">maleficis.</HI> 
 <COL N="0893B"></COL> Et ita habet Cod. Verc.</P> <P COM="0893">42.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cum veneris in regnum tuum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåtan eælqhéû
ejn thðé basileivaé sou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cum veneris in regno tuo:</HI>  et
ita Verc.; Veron. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quando venies in regno tuo.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">48.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et omnis turba.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú pavnteû oæcloi.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et omnes . . . turbae.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">51.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et actibus eorum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú thðé pravxei aujtwðn.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et operae illorum.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">51.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Civitate Judaeae.</HI>  In Graeco:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>povlewû twðn 1Ioudaivwn,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">civitate Judaeorum.</HI>  Et ita in Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0893">56.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Siluerunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJsuvcasan,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quieverunt.</HI>  Et
ita Verc. et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0893">CAP. XXIV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0893">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sabbati.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>sabbavtwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sabbatorum.</HI> 
Et ita Verc. ut Marc. XVI, 2.</P> <P COM="0893">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae paraverant aromata.</HI>  Addunt hic Graeci
codices,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiv tineû suún aujtaiðû.</FOREIGN>  Brixianus quoque,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
uliae simul cum eis.</HI>  Interpres Syrus vertit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et erant
cum eis mulieres aliae.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dum mente consternatae essent.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé
diaporeiðsqai  <COL N="0893C"></COL> aujtaúû.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dum haesitarent.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Verba ista.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú rJhvmata aujtwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">verba
illarum.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0893">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In damnationem mortis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû kriðma,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in
judicium.</HI>  Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in judicio.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ipsum vero non invenerunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoún
deú oujk eiødon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsum vero non viderunt.</HI>  Et ita Corb.,
Veron. et Brix. quibus consonant Verc. et Gat., excepto
quod, pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">vero,</HI>  legunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">autem.</HI>  Cantabrig. habet,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtoún deú oujk eiJdomen,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsum vero non vidimus.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et ita intrare.</HI>  In Graecis libris deest adverbium
illud,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ita;</HI>  ut etiam in Verc.</P> <P COM="0893">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et intravit cum illis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eiJshðlqe touð
meiðnai suún aujtoiðû.</FOREIGN>  Gat.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et intravit manere cum illis.</HI> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et intravit, ut cum eis maneret.</HI>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et intravit
cum illis, ut maneret.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et intravit cum illis, et
mansit.</HI>  Paria in ms. Cantabrig. leguntur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eijshðlqe
touð meiðnai met1 aujtwðn.</FOREIGN>  Quidam mss. Graeci sententiam
hanc totam omittunt.</P> <P COM="0893">30.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et porrigebat illis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejpedivdou aujtoiðû.</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0893D"></COL> Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et dedit eis.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Evanuit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæfantoû ejgevneto.</FOREIGN>  Veron. et
Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">invisus factus.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">32.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dum loqueretur in via.</HI>  Graeci addunt  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hJmiðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nobis.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0893">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae gesta erant in via.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>taú ejn thðé oJdwðé,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quae in via.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0893">36.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Stetit</HI>  JESUS. Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú aujtoúû oJ 1Ihsouðû eæsth.</FOREIGN> 
Gat. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipse autem</HI>  (in Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">autem</HI>  deest)
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Jesus stetit.</HI>  Verc. et Veron.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipse stetit.</HI></P> <P COM="0893">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ascendunt in corda vestra.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn taiðs
kardivaiû uJmwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in cordibus vestris.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0893">41.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Adhuc illis non credentibus, et mirantibus prae
gaudio.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæti deú ajpistouvntwn aujtwðn ajpoú thðû
caraðû, kaiú qaumazovntwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">adhuc autem non credentibus
illis prae gaudio et mirantibus.</HI>  Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0893">43.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et cum manducasset coram eis, sumens reliquias,
dedit eis.</HI>  Graece tantum:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Kaiú labwún, ejnwvpion aujtwðn
 <COL N="0894A"></COL> eæfagen,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et accipiens coram eis manducavit.</HI>  Et
ita Brix. et Verc. Sed Brix. pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">eis,</HI>  legit  <HI REND="ITALIC">ipsis;</HI>  et
Verc. post  <HI REND="ITALIC">manducavit,</HI>  ponit  <HI REND="ITALIC">coram ipsis.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">47.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Incipientibus ab Hierosolyma.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrxavmenon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">incipientem.</HI>  In Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">incipiens.</HI>  In
Cantabrig.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajrxamevnwn.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0894">49.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sedete in civitate.</HI>  Graece additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ierousalhúm,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">in civitate Jerusalem.</HI>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in civitate hac Jerusalem.</HI></P></DIV1> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0894"><HEAD COM="0894">MARCUS.</HEAD> <CAPTION COM="0894">CAP. I.</CAPTION> <P COM="0894">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Universi.</HI>  Et ita solus Brix. Deest vox
illa in libris Graecis.</P> <P COM="0894">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et manentem.</HI>  Deest illud in Graeco, atque in
Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0894">11.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In te complacui.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn wßé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in quo.</HI>  Et ita
Veron. At Cantabrig. habet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn soiú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in te.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et quadraginta noctibus.</HI>  In Graecis libris haec
desunt; ut etiam in Verc., Corb., Veron. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0894">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et credite Evangelio.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn Eujaggelivwé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in
 <COL N="0894B"></COL> Evangelio.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0894">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Relictis retibus.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>auJtwðn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">suis.</HI> 
Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0894">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In proximos vicos, et civitates.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû taúû
ejcomevnaû kwmopovleiû.</FOREIGN>  Verc. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in proxima castella.</HI> 
Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">castella confinia.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">39.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et in omni Galitaea.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû oålhn thún Galilaivan,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">in omnem Galilaeam.</HI>  Et ita Verc. absque,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">44.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Principi sacerdotum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>twðé iJereið,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sacerdoti.</HI> 
Et ita Verc., Veron. et Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0894">CAP. II.</CAPTION> <P COM="0894">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et convenerunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eujqevwû
qunhvcqhsan.</FOREIGN>  In Verc. legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et protinus</HI>  (in Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
confestim) convenerunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et venerunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú eærcontai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et veniunt.</HI>  Et
ita Verc. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0894">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dimittuntur.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajfevwntai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">remissa sunt.</HI>  Et
ita Veron., Brix. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">dimissa sunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Blasphemat.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tiv oußtoû ouåtw laleið,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quid
iste sic loquitur.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0894"><COL N="0894C"></COL> 16.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Magister vester.</HI>  Hae duae voces in Graeco desunt,
ut etiam in Verc., Veron. et Corb.</P> <P COM="0894">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sani.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ ijscuvonteû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fortes.</HI>  Et ita Veron.
Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed peccatores.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû metavnoian.</FOREIGN> 
In Verc. quoque et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in poenitentiam,</HI> 
forte ex Luca additum.</P> <P COM="0894">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sub Abiathar principe sacerdotum.</HI>  Haec desunt
in ms. Cantabrigiensi, atque etiam in Verc., Veron.
et Vind.</P> <CAPTION COM="0894">CAP. III.</CAPTION> <P COM="0894">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Surge in medium.</HI>  Graece in aliquibus
mss.  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejgevrqhti kaiú sthðqi ejn mevswé.</FOREIGN>  In Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">surge,
sta in medium.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">5.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et restituta est manus illi.</HI>  In Graeco additur,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtouð uJgihúû wJû hJ aællh,</FOREIGN>  forte ex Matthaeo. Gat, habet . . .
 <HI REND="ITALIC">illius sanitati, sicut altera.</HI>  Verc. vero, et Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">ejus, sicut et</HI>  (in Veron. deest  <HI REND="ITALIC">et) alia.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Plagas.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mavstigaû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">verbera.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In furorem versus est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejxevsth.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,
Veron., Corb. et Vind. legunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">exsentiat.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Beelzebub.</HI>  Graece est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>Beelzebouúl.</FOREIGN>  Et ita habet
 <COL N="0894D"></COL> Brix. Vind. vero,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Behelzebul;</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Belzebul.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0894">CAP. IV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0894">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et hi, qui cum eo, erant duodecim.</HI> 
Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiJ periú aujtoún suún toiðû dwvdeka.</FOREIGN>  Brix. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hi,
qui cum eo erant cum duodecim.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">18.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et alii sunt.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú oußtoiv eijsin.</FOREIGN>  Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
hi sunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aerumnae.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mevrimnai.</FOREIGN>  Et ita Corb.,
Veron. et Brix. Vind. vero habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sollicitudine.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Saeculi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touð aiwðnoû touvtou,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">saeculi hujus.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0894">24.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et adjicietur vobis.</HI>  Graece additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toiðû ajkouvousi,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">audientibus.</HI>  In Brix. pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">audientibus,</HI>  legitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">credentibus.</HI></P> <P COM="0894">40.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis, putas.</HI>  Graece;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>tivû aæra.</FOREIGN>  Corb. et Vind.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quisnam.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0894">CAP. V.</CAPTION> <P COM="0894">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Occurrit.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aujtwðé,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ei,</HI> 
Et ita in Brix. ac Veron.</P> <P COM="0894"><COL N="0895A"></COL> 10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ne se.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iåna mhú aujtouvû.</FOREIGN>  Brix., Corb. et
Vind. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ne . . . eos.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">12.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Spiritus.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnteû oiJ daivmoneû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">universa daemonia.</HI>  Brix. habet tantum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">daemonia.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Praecipitatus est.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kataú touð krhmnouð.</FOREIGN>  Veron.,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">per praeceps.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">13.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad duo millia.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>høsan gaúr wJû discivlioi.</FOREIGN> 
Verc. videtur legisse,  <HI REND="ITALIC">erant autem circiter duo millia.</HI> 
Brix. et Vind. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">erant autem quasi duo millia.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">34.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vade in pace.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû eijrhvnhn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in pacem.</HI>  Et
ita Vindeb.</P> <CAPTION COM="0895">CAP. VI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0895">2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et virtutes.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti kaiú dunavmeiû.</FOREIGN> 
In Brix. legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod virtutes.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Contristare.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajqethðsai.</FOREIGN>  Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">spernere.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sed.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et.</HI>  Ac ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0895">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et decollavit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ deú ajpelqwún ajpekefavlisen.</FOREIGN> 
Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">isque abiens, decollavit.</HI>  Verc. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et
cum abiisset, decollavit.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">isque abiit, et decollavit.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">35.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et jam hora praeterivit.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú hædh wåra</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0895B"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pollhv.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et hora jam multa,</HI>  etc.</P> <P COM="0895">51.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et plus magis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú livan ejk perissouð.</FOREIGN> 
Veron. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et abundantius.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">Ibid.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Stupebant.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejqauvmazon,</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et mirabantur.</HI>  Et ita habent Veron. et Brix. In Verc.
legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum admiratione.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">56.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In plateis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn taiðû ajgoraiðû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in
foro.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0895">CAP. VII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0895">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Crebro.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pugmhðé.</FOREIGN>  Corb. et
Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pugillo.</HI>  Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">subinde.</HI>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">momento.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et praecepta.</HI>  In Graeco deest,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et:</HI>  ut etiam in
Corb. et Veron.</P> <P COM="0895">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Turbam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>pavnta toún oæclon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">omnem turbam.</HI> 
Et ita Brix.</P> <P COM="0895">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Gentilis.</HI>  In Graeco hic est  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>2Ellhniúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Graeca.</HI>  Et
ita in Verc., Corb. et Vind.</P> <P COM="0895">32.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Mutum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mogivlalon.</FOREIGN>  Gat. habet,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">mugillatum.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fecit audire.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>poieið,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">facit,</HI>  etc. Et ita
 <COL N="0895C"></COL> Verc. ac Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0895">CAP. VIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0895">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Convocatis discipulis.</HI>  In Graeco
additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oJ 1Ihsouðû.</FOREIGN>  Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0895">20.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quot sportas fragmentorum.</HI>  Graece,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>povswn spurivdon
plhrwvmata klasmavtwn.</FOREIGN>  In Brix. legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quot
sportas plenas fragmentorum.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">25.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et coepit videre.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejpoivhsen aujtoún
ajnablevyai,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et fecit eum videre.</HI>  Et ita Brix. et Verc.
(qui tamen pro  <HI REND="ITALIC">eum,</HI>  habet  <HI REND="ITALIC">illum</HI> ).</P> <P COM="0895">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et si in vicum introieris, nemini dixeris.</HI>  Graece,
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mhdeú eijû thún kwvmhn eiJsevlqhés, mhdeú eiæphéû tiniú hjn thðé kwvmhé.</FOREIGN> 
Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ne in municipio intres, neque cuiquam dicas,</HI> 
absque  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn thðé kwvmhé.</FOREIGN></P> <P COM="0895">10.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid ergo dicunt?</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåti levgousin.</FOREIGN>  Veron.
et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia dicunt.</HI></P> <P COM="0895">37.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et prohibuimus eum.</HI>  In Graeco additur:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oujk ajkolouqeið hJmiðn</FOREIGN> ; ut etiam in Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quia non sequitur
nos.</HI>  Veron. vero, et Verc. habent,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui non sequitur
nos</HI>  (Verc.  <HI REND="ITALIC">nobiscum</HI> ).</P> <CAPTION COM="0895">CAP. X.</CAPTION> <P COM="0895">17.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ut vitam aeternam percipiam.</HI>  Graece:
 <COL N="0896A"></COL> <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>klhronomhvso.</FOREIGN>  Verc. et Brix.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">possideam.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">21.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et sequere me.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>aæraû toún
staurovn.</FOREIGN>  In Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sublata cruce.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">29.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aut matrem.</HI>  In Graeco additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>hÞ gunaiðka,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aut
uxorem.</HI>  Et ita in Brix.</P> <P COM="0896">40.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non est meum dare vobis.</HI>  Illud  <HI REND="ITALIC">vobis</HI>  deest in
Graeco, in Verc., Corb., Vindeb. et Veron.</P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. XI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bethaniae.</HI>  In Graeco legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijû
Bhqfaghú kaiú Bhqanivan</FOREIGN>  Brix. habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in Bethfage, et Bethania.</HI> 
Assumentum ex Luca, XIX, 29.</P> <P COM="0896">23.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fiet ei.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eæstai aujtwðé oÝ ejaún eiæph.</FOREIGN>  Verc.
habet,  <HI REND="ITALIC">contingent illi quaecumque dixerit.</HI>  Veron.,
Corb. et Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quodcumque dixerit.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. XII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">6.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Carissimum.</HI>  Graece;  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajgaphtoún</FOREIGN> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">dilectum.</HI>  Et ita Verc.</P> <P COM="0896">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Versutiam.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>uJpovkrisin</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">simulationem.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">26.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ego sum.</HI>  Graecus, et Veron. omittunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sum.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">27.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vivorum.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>zwvntwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">viventium.</HI>  Et ita Gat.</P> <P COM="0896">31.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Secundum autem simile est illi.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú
deutevra oJmoiva auåthé.</FOREIGN> 
 <COL N="0896B"></COL> Veron.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">secundum simile illi.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Cavete a Scribis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>blevpete ajpoú twðn grammatevwn,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">videte a Scribis.</HI>  Et ita Corbeien., Vindebon.
et Veronen.</P> <P COM="0896">38.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui volunt ambulare in stolis, et salutari.</HI>  Graece:
 <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ajspasmouúû,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui volunt ambulare in stolis, et salutationes.</HI> 
Et ita Veron.</P> <P COM="0896">40.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sub obtentu prolixae orationis.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú
profavsei makraðé proseucovmenoi.</FOREIGN>  Verc. et Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">occasione
longa orantes.</HI>  Vind.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">oratione longa orantes.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. XIII.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ubi non debet.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oåpou ouj
degr_ið,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ubi non oportet.</HI>  Et ita Verc. et Corb.</P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. XIV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nardi spicati.</HI>  In Graeco est,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>navrdou
pistikhðû.</FOREIGN>  Et ita in Gat., Brix. et Vindeb. Forte
ex Joanne, cap. XII, 3, ubi legitur,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nardi pistici.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">14.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Refectio mea.</HI>  In Graeco deest pronomen  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>mouð</FOREIGN> 
Et ita in Corb. et Vind.</P> <P COM="0896">15.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Stratum.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eætoimon,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">paratum.</HI> 
Et ita in Corb., Brix et Vindeb.</P> <P COM="0896"><COL N="0896C"></COL> 19.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Numquid ego?</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú aælloû, mhvti
ejgwv,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et alius: Numquid ego?</HI>  Et ita in Corb., Verc.,
Vindeb. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0896">22.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sumite.</HI>  In Graeco Vulgato additur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>favgete</FOREIGN> ; in
Corb.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">edite.</HI>  Non est tamen illud  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>favgete,</FOREIGN>  in mss.
Alexandrino, et Cantabrigiensi.</P> <P COM="0896">34.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et vigilate.</HI>  In Graeco additur  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>met1 ejmouð,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mecum.</HI> 
Et ita in Gat.</P> <P COM="0896">50.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tunc discipuli ejus.</HI>  Non sunt in libris Graecis
haec tria verba, nec in Verc. et Brix.</P> <P COM="0896">56.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et convenientia.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>iøsa,</FOREIGN>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aequalia.</HI>  Et ita
Verc.</P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. XV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fecerat homicidium.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>oiå tineû
ejn thðé stavsei fovnon pepoihvkeisan.</FOREIGN>  Verc. videtur legisse,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">qui in seditione homicidium fecerat.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">8.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et cum ascendisset turba.</HI>  Graece:  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ajnabohvsaû
oJ oæcloû.</FOREIGN>  Verc.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">accensa tota turba:</HI>  quae lectio
magis videtur accedere ad  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnabovhsaû</FOREIGN>  (licet  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnaboaðén,</FOREIGN> 
significet  <HI REND="ITALIC">exclamare</HI> ), quam ad  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ajnabhvsaû,</FOREIGN>  quod interpretatur,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">cum ascendisset.</HI></P></DIV1></DOC> <DOC NAME="Concordantes lectiones cum Graecis codicibus" AUTHOR="Auctor incertus" STATUS=S TEMPSTAT=UNCERT SECOND=YES COM="0896"><COL N="0895"></COL> <HEAD TYPE=main COM="0895">CONCORDANTES LECTIONES.
EVANGELIARII QUADRUPLICIS
CUM DECEM GRAECIS CODICIBUS MSS. ROMAE ASSERVATIS.</HEAD> <DIV1 SECOND=YES COM="0895"><HEAD COM="0895">S. MATTHAEUS.</HEAD> <COL N="0895C"></COL> <CAPTION COM="0895">CAP. I.</CAPTION> <P COM="0895">10. Ms. 1,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>toún 3Amoû,</FOREIGN>  cum Cor.</P> <P COM="0895">25. Ms. 1,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eåwû ouß eæteken uiJoún kaiú ejkavlese,</FOREIGN>  cum Veron.
et San-Ger.</P> <CAPTION COM="0895">CAP. IV.</CAPTION> <P COM="0895">16. Ms. I,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú toiðû kaqhmevnoiû ejn skovtei
kaiú skiaðé.</FOREIGN>  Cor. legit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sedentibus in regione, et umbra.</HI></P> <P COM="0895"><COL N="0896C"></COL> 24. Ms. 1,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>kaiú ejxhðlqen hJ ajkohv.</FOREIGN>  San-Ger.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fama.</HI></P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. V.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">22. In ms. 9, habetur vox  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>eijkhð,</FOREIGN>  cum
Verc., Veron., Corb. et Brix,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sine causa.</HI></P> <P COM="0896">47. Mss. 9,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>touúû fivlouû uJmwðn,</FOREIGN>  cum Brix.</P> <CAPTION COM="0896">CAP. VI.</CAPTION> <P COM="0896">4 et 6. In mss. 9 legitur,  <FOREIGN LANG=Greek>ejn twðé fanerwðé.</FOREIGN> 
In Verc. et San-Ger.,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in palum</HI>  (sed in San-Ger. se-
